{
  "title": "4: al-Nisaa النساء",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ اتَّقُوْا رَبَّكُمُ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَكُمْ مِّنْ نَّفْسٍ وَّاحِدَةٍ وَّخَلَقَ مِنْهَا زَوْجَهَا وَبَثَّ مِنْهُمَا رِجَالًا كَثِيْرًا وَّنِسَآءً ۚ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ الَّذِىْ تَسَآءَلُوْنَ بِهٖ وَالْاَرْحَامَ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ عَلَيْكُمْ رَقِيْبًا‏(1)\nYAA AYYOHAL NAASO TAQOO RABBAKOMUL LAZEE KHALAQAKUM MIN NAFSIN WWAAHEDATIN WWAKHALAQA MINHAA ZAWJAHAA WA BASSA MINHOMAA REJAALAN KASEERAA WWANESAAAN WAT TAQUL LAAHA LAZEE TASAAALOONA BEHI WAL AARHAAMA INNAL LAAHA KAANA A’LAYKUM RAQEEBAN.\nO’ men! take shelter in your Lord Who hath created you from a single self and created from it, its pair, and spread from these two, men manifold and women, and fear God, in Whose name ye importune one another, and (be mindful’) of kinship; Verily God is vigilant over you.\nوَاٰ تُوا الْيَتٰمٰٓى اَمْوَالَهُمْ وَلَا تَتَبَدَّلُوا الْخَبِيْثَ بِالطَّيِّبِ وَلَا تَاْكُلُوْۤا اَمْوَالَهُمْ اِلٰٓى اَمْوَالِكُمْؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ حُوْبًا كَبِيْرًا‏‏(2)\nWAA TOOA AL-YATAAMAAA AMWAALAHUM WA LAA TATABADDALOOA KHABEESA BEALTTAYBE WA LAA TAAKULOOA AMWAALAHUM ELAA AAMWAALEKUM INNAHU KAANA HOOBAN KABEERAA.\nAnd give unto orphans their property, and substitute not (your) worthless things for (their) good ones, and devour not ye their property, along with your own; for verily it is a great crime.\nوَاِنْ خِفْتُمْ اَلَّا تُقْسِطُوْا فِى الْيَتٰمٰى فَانْكِحُوْا مَا طَابَ لَكُمْ مِّنَ النِّسَآءِ مَثْنٰى وَثُلٰثَ وَرُبٰعَ ۚ فَاِنْ خِفْتُمْ اَلَّا تَعْدِلُوْا فَوَاحِدَةً اَوْ مَا مَلَكَتْ اَيْمَانُكُمْ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ اَدْنٰٓى اَلَّا تَعُوْلُوْا ؕ‏(3)\nWA KHIFTUM ALLAA TUQSETOOA FIL AL-YATAAMAA FAANKEHOOA MAA TAABA LAKUM MENAL NESAAA-E MASNAA WASULAASA WARUBAAA’A FA-IN KHIFTUM ALLAA TAA’DELOOA FAWAAHEDATAN AW MAA MALAKAT AYMAANOKUM ZAA LEKA TAQARRA ALLAA TAU’OOLOOA.\nAnd if ye fear that ye cannot act justly among the orphans then marry those who seem good to you, two, or three or four, and if ye fear that ye shall not deal justly (with so many) then (marry) one only, or (the slave women) whom your right hands have acquired; that is nigh keeping you from transgressing.\nوَاٰ تُوا النِّسَآءَ صَدُقٰتِهِنَّ نِحْلَةً ؕ فَاِنْ طِبْنَ لَكُمْ عَنْ شَىْءٍ مِّنْهُ نَفْسًا فَكُلُوْهُ هَنِيْٓئًا مَّرِیْٓٴًﺎ‏(4)\nWAA TOOA NESAAA-A SADUQAATEHENNA NEHLATAN FA-IN TEBNA LAKUM A’N SHAY-IN MINHO NAFSAN FAKULOOHU HANEEAN MMARE.\nGive away women their dowry freely (without any restraint)’, but if, they of themselves (voluntarily with pleasure) remit unto you anything thereof, then (ye may) consume it with pleasure (and it shall be) wholesome (to you).\nوَلَا تُؤْتُوا السُّفَهَآءَ اَمْوَالَكُمُ الَّتِىْ جَعَلَ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ قِيٰمًا وَّارْزُقُوْهُمْ فِيْهَا وَاكْسُوْهُمْ وَقُوْلُوْا لَهُمْ قَوْلًا مَّعْرُوْفًا‏(5)\nWA LAA TUTOOA AS-SUFAHAAA AAMWAALAKUMU LATEE JA-A’LA LAAHO LAKUM QEEMAN WWAARZUQOOHUM FEEHAA WAAKSOOHUM WA QOOLOO LAHUM QAWLAM MA’ROOFAA.\nAnd give not away to the weak in mind, your property which God hath made for you (a means of) your sustenance but maintain them therewith, and clothe them, and speak to them with kind words (for their good) ”.\nوَابْتَلُوا الْيَتٰمٰى حَتّٰىۤ اِذَا بَلَغُوا النِّكَاحَ ۚ فَاِنْ اٰنَسْتُمْ مِّنْهُمْ رُشْدًا فَادْفَعُوْۤا اِلَيْهِمْ اَمْوَالَهُمْۚ وَلَا تَاْكُلُوْهَاۤ اِسْرَافًا وَّبِدَارًا اَنْ يَّكْبَرُوْا ؕ وَمَنْ كَانَ غَنِيًّا فَلْيَسْتَعْفِفْ ۚ وَمَنْ كَانَ فَقِيْرًا فَلْيَاْكُلْ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ ؕ فَاِذَا دَفَعْتُمْ اِلَيْهِمْ اَمْوَالَهُمْ فَاَشْهِدُوْا عَلَيْهِمْ ؕ وَكَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ حَسِيْبًا‏(6)\nWAABTALOOA AL-YATAAMAA HATTAA EZAA BALAGHOOA AN-NEKAAHA FA-IN AAANASTUM MINHUM RUSHDAN FAADFAU’OOA ELAYHIM AMWAALAHUM WA LAA TAAKULOOHAA AESRAAFAN WWABEDAARAN AN YYAKBAROOA WA MAN KAANA GHANEEA FALYASTAA’FEF WA MAN KAANA FAQEERAN FALYAAKUL BIL-MA’ROOF FA-EZAA DAFAA’TUM ELAYHIM AMWAALAHUM FAASHHEDOOA A’LAYHIM KAFAA BIL-LAAHE HASEEBAA.\nAnd test the orphans until they reach (age marriageable) if ye find in them maturity, then make over to them their property, and consume it not wastefully and hastily lest they grow to full age; and he (the guardian) who is rich, let him abstain (altogether) and he who is poor let him consume (eat) (for) (himself) reasonably; And when ye make over to them their property let there be witnesses on them (in their presence); And God is enough a Reckoner.\nلِلرِّجَالِ نَصِيْبٌ مِّمَّا تَرَكَ الْوَالِدٰنِ وَالْاَقْرَبُوْنَ وَلِلنِّسَآءِ نَصِيْبٌ مِّمَّا تَرَكَ الْوَالِدٰنِ وَالْاَقْرَبُوْنَ مِمَّا قَلَّ مِنْهُ اَوْ كَثُرَ ؕ نَصِيْبًا مَّفْرُوْضًا‏(7)\nLELRREJAALE NASEEBUM MIMMAA TARAKA AL-WAALEDAANE WAL AAQRABOONA WALELNNESAAE NASEEBUM MIMMAA TARAKA AL-WAALEDAANE WAL AAQRABOONA MIMMAA QALLA MINHO AW KASURA NASEEBAN MMAFROOZAN.\nFor men shall be a share in what their parents and kindred leave and for women shall be a share in what their parents and kindred leave, be it little or much; (It is) a decreed (allotment of) share.\nوَاِذَا حَضَرَ الْقِسْمَةَ اُولُوا الْقُرْبٰى وَالْيَتٰمٰى وَالْمَسٰكِيْنُ فَارْزُقُوْهُمْ مِّنْهُ وَقُوْلُوْا لَهُمْ قَوْلًا مَّعْرُوْفًا‏(8)\nWA EZAA HAZARA AL-QESMATA ULUL QURBAA WAL YATAAMAA WAL MASAAKEENU FAARZUQOOHUM MINHO WA QOOLOO LAHUM QAWLAM MA’ROOFAA.\nAnd when at the division are present those of kin, and orphans and the needy, provide them also with (something) from it, And speak to them kind words.\nوَلْيَخْشَ الَّذِيْنَ لَوْ تَرَكُوْا مِنْ خَلْفِهِمْ ذُرِّيَّةً ضِعٰفًا خَافُوْا عَلَيْهِمْ فَلْيَتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَلْيَقُوْلُوا قَوْلًا سَدِيْدًا‏(9)\nWALYAKHSHA LAZEENA LAW TARAKOO MIN KHALFEHIM ZURREETAN ZEA’AAFAN KHAAFOOA A’LAYHIM FALYATTAQOOA LAAHA WALYAQOOLOOA QAWLAM SADEEDAY.\nAnd let those fear (against hurting the Orphans) who, should they leave behind them weakly offspring, would fear on their account, so let them fear God and let them speak the right words.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يَاْكُلُوْنَ اَمْوَالَ الْيَتٰمٰى ظُلْمًا اِنَّمَا يَاْكُلُوْنَ فِىْ بُطُوْنِهِمْ نَارًا ؕ وَسَيَصْلَوْنَ سَعِيْرًا‏(10)\nINNAL LAZEENA YAAKOLOON AAMWAALA AL-YATAAMAA ZULMAWN INNAMAA YAAKOLOON FEE BOTOONEHIM NAARAN WASAYASLAWNA SA-E’ERAA.\nVerily, those who eat away the properties of the orphans unjustly, they swallow (only) fire into their bellies; and anon shall they enter the blazing Hell-fire.\nيُوْصِيْكُمُ اللّٰهُ فِىْۤ اَوْلَادِكُمْ لِلذَّكَرِ مِثْلُ حَظِّ الْاُنْثَيَيْنِ ۚ فَاِنْ كُنَّ نِسَآءً فَوْقَ اثْنَتَيْنِ فَلَهُنَّ ثُلُثَا مَا تَرَكَ ۚ وَاِنْ كَانَتْ وَاحِدَةً فَلَهَا النِّصْفُ ؕ وَلِاَ بَوَيْهِ لِكُلِّ وَاحِدٍ مِّنْهُمَا السُّدُسُ مِمَّا تَرَكَ اِنْ كَانَ لَهٗ وَلَدٌ ۚ فَاِنْ لَّمْ يَكُنْ لَّهٗ وَلَدٌ وَّوَرِثَهٗۤ اَبَوٰهُ فَلِاُمِّهِ الثُّلُثُ ؕ فَاِنْ كَانَ لَهٗۤ اِخْوَةٌ فَلِاُمِّهِ السُّدُسُ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ وَصِيَّةٍ يُّوْصِىْ بِهَاۤ اَوْ دَيْنٍ ؕ اٰبَآؤُكُمْ وَاَبْنَآؤُكُمْ ۚ لَا تَدْرُوْنَ اَيُّهُمْ اَقْرَبُ لَكُمْ نَفْعًا ؕ فَرِيْضَةً مِّنَ اللّٰهِ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ عَلِيْمًا حَكِيْمًا‏(11)\nYOOSEEKUMU LAAHO FEE AAWLAADEKUM LELZZAKARE LAZEE HAZZE AL-AUNSAYAYNE FA-IN KUNNA NESAAAN FAWQA ASNATAYNE FA LAHUNNA SULUSAA MAA TARAKA WA KAANAT WAAHEDATAN FA LAHAA AN-NESFU WALEAA BAWAYHE LEKULLIM WAAHEDIN MINHOMAA WA AS-SUDUSU MIMMAA TARAKA IN KAANA LAHU WALADUN FA-IN LAM YAKUL LAHU WALADUN WWAWARESAH AABAWHU FALEAUMMEHE AS-SULUSU FA-IN KAANA LAHU AEKHWATUN FALEAUMMEHE AS-SUDUSU MIN BA’DE WASEETIN YYOOSEAA BEHAA AW DAYNIN AAABAAUKUM WAABNAAUKUM LAA TADROONA AAYHUM AQRABO LAKUM BEKUM FAREEZATANW MENAL LAAHE INNAL LAAHA KAANA A’LEEMAN HAKEEMAA.\nGod enjoineth you about your issues! the male shall have the equal of the shares of two females and if they be females (only two and) more than two, then they shall have two thirds of that which (the deceased) hath left; but if she be an only daughter, she shall have the half; and the father and the mother of the deceased shall each of them have a sixth part of what he hath left if he hath an issue but if he hath no issue and his parents be his heirs then his mother shall have the third; and if he hath brethren his mother shall have the sixth, after paying the bequest he shall have bequeathed and his debt; As to your father or your issues, ye know not which of them is the most advantageous to you; (these assignments are) an ordinance from God; Verily, God is All Knowing, All-Wise.\nوَلَكُمْ نِصْفُ مَا تَرَكَ اَزْوَاجُكُمْ اِنْ لَّمْ يَكُنْ لَّهُنَّ وَلَدٌ ۚ فَاِنْ كَانَ لَهُنَّ وَلَدٌ فَلَكُمُ الرُّبُعُ مِمَّا تَرَكْنَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ وَصِيَّةٍ يُّوْصِيْنَ بِهَاۤ اَوْ دَ يْنٍ ؕ وَلَهُنَّ الرُّبُعُ مِمَّا تَرَكْتُمْ اِنْ لَّمْ يَكُنْ لَّكُمْ وَلَدٌ ۚ فَاِنْ كَانَ لَكُمْ وَلَدٌ فَلَهُنَّ الثُّمُنُ مِمَّا تَرَكْتُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ وَصِيَّةٍ تُوْصُوْنَ بِهَاۤ اَوْ دَ يْنٍ ؕ وَاِنْ كَانَ رَجُلٌ يُّوْرَثُ كَلٰلَةً اَوِ امْرَاَةٌ وَّلَهٗۤ اَخٌ اَوْ اُخْتٌ فَلِكُلِّ وَاحِدٍ مِّنْهُمَا السُّدُسُ ۚ فَاِنْ كَانُوْۤا اَكْثَرَ مِنْ ذٰ لِكَ فَهُمْ شُرَكَآءُ فِى الثُّلُثِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ وَصِيَّةٍ يُّوْصٰى بِهَاۤ اَوْ دَ يْنٍ ۙ غَيْرَ مُضَآرٍّ ۚ وَصِيَّةً مِّنَ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَلِيْمٌ ؕ‏(12)\nWA LAKUM NESFU MAA TARAKA AAZWAAJUKUM IN LAM YAKUL LEBAASUL WALADUN FA-IN KAANA LAHUNNA WALADUN FA LAKOMUL AR-RUBUU’U MIMMAA TARAKNA MIN BA’DE WASEETIN YYOOSEENA BEHAA AW DA YNIN MISLUL AR-RUBUU’U MIMMAA TARAKTUM IN LAM YAKUL LAKUM WALADUN FA-IN KAANA LAKUM WALADUN FA LAHUNNA AS-SUMUNU MIMMAA TARAKTUM MIN BA’DE WASEETIN TOOSOONA BEHAA AW DA YNIN WA KAANA RAJOLUM YYOORASU KALAALATAN AWE’ AMRAATUN WWALAH AAKHUN AW AUKHTUN FA LEKULLIM WAAHEDIN MINHOMAA WA AS-SUDUSU FA-IN KAANOO AKSARAN MIN ZAA LEKA FAHUM SHURAKAAU FIL AS-SULUSE MIN BA’DE WASEETIN YYOOSAA BEHAA AW DA YNIN GHAYRA MUZAARRIN WASEETAN MENAL LAAHE WAL LAAHO A’LEEM HALEEM.\nFor you, shall be half of what leave your wives if they have no issue, but if they have an issue, then for you shall be a fourth of what they leave after paying the bequest they had bequeathed and the debt; And for them shall be a fourth of what ye leave if ye have no issue, and if ye have an issue then for them (shall be) the eighth of what ye leave after paying the bequest ye had bequeathed and the debt; and if a man or woman leaveth (his property) to be inherited by (not the lineage but) any side relation and he or she hath a brother or a sister each of these two shall have the sixth; but if there be more than this, then they shall be sharers in the (one) third after (paying) the bequest he had bequeathed, and the debt, without loss (to anyone); this is an Ordinance from God; and Verily, God is All-Knowing, the Most Forbearing.\nتِلْكَ حُدُوْدُ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَمَنْ يُّطِعِ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ يُدْخِلْهُ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا ؕ وَذٰ لِكَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(13)\nTILKA TILKA LAAHE WA MAN YOTE-I’L LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU YUDKHILHO JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA WAZAA LEKA FAWZUL A’ZEEM.\nThese are the limits set by God; and whoso obeyeth God and His Apostle (Muhammad), him will God admit into gardens beneath which flow rivers to abide therein for ever; and this is a Great Achievement.\nوَمَنْ يَّعْصِ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ وَيَتَعَدَّ حُدُوْدَهٗ يُدْخِلْهُ نَارًا خَالِدًا فِيْهَا وَلَهٗ عَذَابٌ مُّهِيْنٌ‏(14)\nWA MAN YA’ASIL LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU WAYATAA’ADDA HUDOODAH YUDKHILHO NAARAN KHAALEDAN FEEHAA WA LAHU A’ZAABUN MOHEEN.\nAnd whoso disobeyeth God and His Apostle (Muhammad) and transgresseth His limits, him shall God admit in Hell-fire, to abide therein and for him shall be a shameful torment.\nوَالّٰتِىْ يَاْتِيْنَ الْفَاحِشَةَ مِنْ نِّسَآئِكُمْ فَاسْتَشْهِدُوْا عَلَيْهِنَّ اَرْبَعَةً مِّنْكُمْ ۚ فَاِنْ شَهِدُوْا فَاَمْسِكُوْهُنَّ فِى الْبُيُوْتِ حَتّٰى يَتَوَفّٰٮهُنَّ الْمَوْتُ اَوْ يَجْعَلَ اللّٰهُ لَهُنَّ سَبِيْلًا‏(15)\nWA KHAALEKA YAATEENA FAAHESHATA MIN NESAAA-EKUM FAASTASHHEDOOA A’LAYHINNA ARBA-A’TAM MINKUM FA-IN SHAHEDOOA FA-AMSEKOOHUNNA FIL AL-BUYOOTE HATTAA YATAWAFFAAHUNNA MAWTO AW YAJA’ALA LAAHO LAHUNNA SABEELAA.\nAnd as to such of those who are guilty of lewdness from among your women, then bring four witnesses against them from among yourselves; and if they bear witness (to the fact), Confine them to the houses till death taketh them away or God maketh some way for them.\nوَالَّذٰنِ يَاْتِيٰنِهَا مِنْكُمْ فَاٰذُوْهُمَا ۚ فَاِنْ تَابَا وَاَصْلَحَا فَاَعْرِضُوْا عَنْهُمَا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ تَوَّابًا رَّحِيْمًا‏(16)\nWAALLAZAANE YAATEENEHAA MINKUM FAAZOOHUMAA FA-IN TAABAA WAASLAHAA FAAA’REZOOA A’ANHUMAA INNAL LAAHA KAANA TAWWAABAA RAHEEMAA.\nAnd if a couple among you commit it (lewdness) chastise them both, then if they (both) repent and amend, then, turn ye away from them; Verily, God is Oft-returning (to Mercy), the Merciful.\nاِنَّمَا التَّوْبَةُ عَلَى اللّٰهِ لِلَّذِيْنَ يَعْمَلُوْنَ السُّوْٓءَ بِجَهَالَةٍ ثُمَّ يَتُوْبُوْنَ مِنْ قَرِيْبٍ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ يَتُوْبُ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِمْؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ عَلِيْمًا حَكِيْمًا‏(17)\nINNAMAA AT-TAWBATU A’LAL LAAHE LILLAZEENA YA’MALOON AS-SOOA BEJAHAALATIN SUMMA YATOOBOONA MIN QAREEBIN FA-OOLAAA-EKA YATOOBU LAAHO WA KAANAL LAAHO A’LEEMAN HAKEEMAA.\nVerily, repentance (acceptable) with God is only for those who do evil ignorantly and then turn (unto God) soon (after)’, These! (are those) God will turn (merciful) unto them; And God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.\nوَلَيْسَتِ التَّوْبَةُ لِلَّذِيْنَ يَعْمَلُوْنَ السَّيِّاٰتِ ۚ حَتّٰۤى اِذَا حَضَرَ اَحَدَهُمُ الْمَوْتُ قَالَ اِنِّىْ تُبْتُ الْئٰنَ وَلَا الَّذِيْنَ يَمُوْتُوْنَ وَهُمْ كُفَّارٌ ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ اَعْتَدْنَا لَهُمْ عَذَابًا اَ لِيْمًا‏(18)\nWA LAYSATIL AT-TAWBATU LILLAZEENA YA’MALOON SAYYE-AATE HATTAA EZAA HAZARA AAHADAHUMU MAWTO QAALA INNEE TUBTU AL-AANA WA LAA LAZEENA YAMOOTOONA WA HUM KUFFAARUN OOLAAA-EKA A-A’TADNAA LAHUM A’ZAABAN A’ZAABAN ALEEMAA.\nAnd repentance is not (profitable) for those who do evil until death cometh to one of them, he saith “Now surely am I turned unto God,” nor (is repentance profitable) for those who die while they are unbelievers; These, for them we have made ready a grievous torment!\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا يَحِلُّ لَكُمْ اَنْ تَرِثُوا النِّسَآءَ كَرْهًا ؕ وَلَا تَعْضُلُوْهُنَّ لِتَذْهَبُوْا بِبَعْضِ مَاۤ اٰتَيْتُمُوْهُنَّ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّاْتِيْنَ بِفَاحِشَةٍ مُّبَيِّنَةٍ ۚ وَعَاشِرُوْهُنَّ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ ۚ فَاِنْ كَرِهْتُمُوْهُنَّ فَعَسٰۤى اَنْ تَكْرَهُوْا شَيْئًا وَّيَجْعَلَ اللّٰهُ فِيْهِ خَيْرًا كَثِيْرًا‏(19)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA YAHILLO LAKUM AN TARESOOA NESAAA-A AW WA LAA TA’ZOLOOHUNNA LETAZHABOOA BE-BA’ZIL MAA MIMMAA ILLAA AN YAKHRUJNA MINKUNNA BE-FAAHESHATIM WAA’AASHEROOHUNNA BIL-MA’ROOF FA-IN KAREHTUMOOHUNNA FA A’SAA AN TAKRAHOO SHAY-ANW WWAYAJA’ALA LAAHO FEEHE KHAYRAN KASEERAA.\nO’ those who believe! It is not lawful for you to inherit women against their will; and do not straiten them in order that ye may take a part of what ye have given them, unless they are guilty of manifest lewdness; but deal kindly with them, and if ye hate them, it may be that ye hate a thing while God hath placed in it abundant good.\nوَاِنْ اَرَدتُّمُ اسْتِبْدَالَ زَوْجٍ مَّكَانَ زَوْجٍ ۙ وَّاٰتَيْتُمْ اِحْدٰٮهُنَّ قِنْطَارًا فَلَا تَاْخُذُوْا مِنْهُ شَيْئًا ؕ اَ تَاْخُذُوْنَهٗ بُهْتَانًا وَّاِثْمًا مُّبِيْنًا‏(20)\nWA AARADTTUMU ASTEBDAALA ZAWJIN MMAKAANA ZAWJIN WWAATAYTUM AEHDAAHUNNA QENTAARAN FALAA AN MINHO SHAY-ANW A’ZAABAN TAAKHUZOONAH BOHTAANANW WA ISMAM MOBEENAA.\nAnd if ye intend to take one wife in place of another, and have given one of them a heap of gold, then take not from it anything; Would you take it by slandering (her) and with manifest wrong?\nوَ كَيْفَ تَاْخُذُوْنَهٗ وَقَدْ اَفْضٰى بَعْضُكُمْ اِلٰى بَعْضٍ وَّاَخَذْنَ مِنْكُمْ مِّيْثَاقًا غَلِيْظًا‏(21)\nWA KAYFA TAAKHUZOONAH WA QAD AAFZAA BA’ZOKUM ELAA ELAA WWAAKHAZNA MINKUM MMEESAAQAN GHALEEZAA.\nAnd how could ye take it when one of you hath gone in unto the other and they have taken from you a firm covenant.\nوَلَا تَنْكِحُوْا مَا نَكَحَ اٰبَآؤُكُمْ مِّنَ النِّسَآءِ اِلَّا مَا قَدْ سَلَفَ ؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ فَاحِشَةً وَّمَقْتًا ؕ وَسَآءَ سَبِيْلًا‏(22)\nWA LAA LAA MAA NAKAHA AAABAAUKUM MENAL NESAAA-E ILLAA MAA QAD SALAFA INNAHU KAANA FAAHESHATAN WWAMAQTAN WA SAAA-A SABEELAA.\nAnd marry not women whom your fathers have married, except what hath already passed; for it is shameful, and abominable; and an evil way.\nحُرِّمَتْ عَلَيْكُمْ اُمَّهٰتُكُمْ وَبَنٰتُكُمْ وَاَخَوٰتُكُمْ وَعَمّٰتُكُمْ وَخٰلٰتُكُمْ وَبَنٰتُ الْاٰخِ وَبَنٰتُ الْاُخْتِ وَاُمَّهٰتُكُمُ الّٰتِىْۤ اَرْضَعْنَكُمْ وَاَخَوٰتُكُمْ مِّنَ الرَّضَاعَةِ وَ اُمَّهٰتُ نِسَآئِكُمْ وَرَبَآئِبُكُمُ الّٰتِىْ فِىْ حُجُوْرِكُمْ مِّنْ نِّسَآئِكُمُ الّٰتِىْ دَخَلْتُمْ بِهِنَّ فَاِنْ لَّمْ تَكُوْنُوْا دَخَلْتُمْ بِهِنَّ فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكُمْ وَحَلَاۤئِلُ اَبْنَآئِكُمُ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ اَصْلَابِكُمْۙ وَاَنْ تَجْمَعُوْا بَيْنَ الْاُخْتَيْنِ اِلَّا مَا قَدْ سَلَفَؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ غَفُوْرًا رَّحِيْمًا ۙ‏(23)\nHURREMAT A’LAYKUM AUMMAHAATUKUM WABANAATUKUM WAAKHAWTUKUM WAA’AMMAATUKUM WAKHAALAATUKUM WABANAATU AL-AAAKHE WABANAATU AL-AUKHTE WAAMMAHAATUKUMU KHAALEKA AARZAA’NAKUM WAAKHAWTUKUM MENAL AR-RAZAAA’ATE WA AUMMAHAATU NESAAEKUM WARABAAAEBUKUMU KHAALEKA FEE HUJOOREKUM MIN NNESAAEKUMU KHAALEKA DAKHALTUM BEHINNA FA-IN LAM TAKOONOO DAKHALTUM BEHINNA FALAA JONAAHA A’LAYKUM WAHALAAELU AABNAAEKUMU LAZEENA MIN AASLAABEKUM WA TAJMAU’OOA BAYNA AL-AUKHTAYNE ILLAA MAA QAD SALAF INNAL LAAHA KAANA GHAFOORAR RAHEEMAA.\nForbidden to you are your mothers, and your daughters, and your sisters, and your aunts paternal and aunts maternal, and daughters of your brother and daughters of your sister, and your foster mothers and your foster sisters, and the mothers of your wives and your step-daughters in your guardianship, (born) of your wives to whom ye have gone in; but if ye have not gone in to them it shall not be a sin on you (to marry them), and the wives of your sons who proceed from your loins and that ye combine two sisters (at one and the same time in the wedlock), except what hath already passed; Verily, God is Oft-Forgiving, Merciful.\nوَّالْمُحْصَنٰتُ مِنَ النِّسَآءِ اِلَّا مَا مَلَكَتْ اَيْمَانُكُمْۚ كِتٰبَ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكُمْۚ وَاُحِلَّ لَكُمْ مَّا وَرَآءَ ذٰ لِكُمْ اَنْ تَبْتَغُوْا بِاَمْوَالِكُمْ مُّحْصِنِيْنَ غَيْرَ مُسَافِحِيْنَ ؕ فَمَا اسْتَمْتَعْتُمْ بِهٖ مِنْهُنَّ فَاٰ تُوْهُنَّ اُجُوْرَهُنَّ فَرِيْضَةً ؕ وَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكُمْ فِيْمَا تَرٰضَيْتُمْ بِهٖ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ الْفَرِيْضَةِ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ عَلِيْمًا حَكِيْمًا‏(24)\nWWAALMUHSANAATU MENAL NESAAA-E ILLAA MAA MALAKAT AYMAANOKUM KETAABAL LAAHE A’LAYKUM WA OHILLA LAKUM MAA WARAAA-A ZAA ZAALEKUM AN TABTAGHOO BE-ANWAALEKUM MMUHSENEENA GHAYRA MUSAAFEHEENA FAMAA ASTAMTAA’TUM BEHI MINHUNNA FA-AATOOHUNNA OJOORAHUN OJOORAHUNNA FAREEZATANW WA LAA JONAAHA A’LAYKUM FEEMAA TARAAZAYTUM BEHI MIN BA’DE AL-FAREEZATE INNAL LAAHA KAANA A’LEEMAN HAKEEMAA.\nAnd (all) protected (married) ones of the women (are forbidden unto you) save those whom your right hands possess. (This is) God’s written ordinance unto you; And it is allowed for you, (all women) besides these that ye may seek (them) by means of your wealth taking (them) into marriage and not committing fornication; and as such of them ye had Mut’a ’ with them, give them their dowries as a fixed reward; and it shall not be a sin on you, in whatever ye mutually agree (to vary) after the fixed reward; Verily God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.\nوَمَنْ لَّمْ يَسْتَطِعْ مِنْكُمْ طَوْلًا اَنْ يَّنْكِحَ الْمُحْصَنٰتِ الْمُؤْمِنٰتِ فَمِنْ مَّا مَلَكَتْ اَيْمَانُكُمْ مِّنْ فَتَيٰتِكُمُ الْمُؤْمِنٰتِ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ اَعْلَمُ بِاِيْمَانِكُمْ ؕ بَعْضُكُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْضٍ ۚ فَانْكِحُوْهُنَّ بِاِذْنِ اَهْلِهِنَّ وَاٰ تُوْهُنَّ اُجُوْرَهُنَّ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ مُحْصَنٰتٍ غَيْرَ مُسٰفِحٰتٍ وَّلَا مُتَّخِذٰتِ اَخْدَانٍ ؕ فَاِذَاۤ اُحْصِنَّ فَاِنْ اَ تَيْنَ بِفَاحِشَةٍ فَعَلَيْهِنَّ نِصْفُ مَا عَلَى الْمُحْصَنٰتِ مِنَ الْعَذَابِ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ لِمَنْ خَشِىَ الْعَنَتَ مِنْكُمْ ؕ وَاَنْ تَصْبِرُوْا خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(25)\nWA MAN LAM YASTATEA’ MINKUM TAWLAN AN YYANKEHA AL-MUHSANAATE MOAMENAATE FAMIN MAA MALAKAT AYMAANOKUM MIN FATAYTEKUMU MOAMENAATE WAL LAAHO A-A’LAMO BE-EEMAANEKUM BA’ZOKUM MIN ELAA FAANKEHOOHUNNA BE-IZNIL AAHLEHENNA WAA OJOORAHUN OJOORAHUNNA BIL-MA’ROOF MUHSANAATIN GHAYRA MUSAAFEHAATIN WA LAA MUTTAKHEZAATE AAKHDAANIN FA-EZAA AUHSENNA FA-IN A’ZAABAN TAYNA MINKUNNA FA A’LAYHINNA NESFU MAA A’LAL AL-MUHSANAATE MENAL A’ZAABE ZAA LEKA LEMAN-Y KHASHEAAA AL-A’ANATA MINKUM WA TASBEROOA KHAYRUL LAKUM WAL LAAHO GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nAnd whoever of you hath not means enough to marry protected believing women, then (let him marry) from among those whom your right hands possess (as slaves or captives) from among your believing maidens; and verily God better knoweth your faith; Ye are (sprung) one from the other, so marry them, with the permission of their masters, and give them their dowries (which may be) in fairness, their getting protected not committing lewd-ness, nor receiving paramours (secretly), And after they are protected (under a Wedlock) and then if they are proved guilty of lewdness, then on them shall be half the punishment (prescribed) for the free women; This (Permission) is for him among you who feareth his falling into evil; and that ye be self-restraint is better for you; Verily, God is Oft-Forgiving, All- Merciful.\nيُرِيْدُ اللّٰهُ لِيُبَيِّنَ لَكُمْ وَيَهْدِيَكُمْ سُنَنَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ وَيَتُوْبَ عَلَيْكُمْ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(26)\nYOREEDO LAAHO LEEBAYNA LAKUM WA YAHDEYAKUM SUNANA LAZEENA MIN QABLEKUM WA YATOOBAL A’LAYKUM WAL LAAHO A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nGod desireth to explain to you (His Ordinances) and to guide you in the ways of those (gone) before you and to turn (mercifully) unto you; for God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.\nوَاللّٰهُ يُرِيْدُ اَنْ يَّتُوْبَ عَلَيْكُمْ وَيُرِيْدُ الَّذِيْنَ يَتَّبِعُوْنَ الشَّهَوٰتِ اَنْ تَمِيْلُوْا مَيْلًا عَظِيْمًا‏(27)\nWAL LAAHO YOREEDO AN YYATOOBA A’LAYKUM WA YOREEDO LAZEENA YATTABEU’OONA ASH-SHAHAWTE AN TAMEELOOA MAYLAN A’ZEEMAA.\nVerily God desireth to turn (Merciful) unto you; but desireth those who follow their own lusts that ye should deviate a great deviation.\nيُرِيْدُ اللّٰهُ اَنْ يُّخَفِّفَ عَنْكُمْۚ وَخُلِقَ الْاِنْسَانُ ضَعِيْفًا‏(28)\nYOREEDO LAAHO AN YYUKHAFFEFA A’NKUM WA KHOLEQA INSAANO HAQQO.\nGod desireth to lighten your burden, and man hath been created weak.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَاْكُلُوْۤا اَمْوَالَكُمْ بَيْنَكُمْ بِالْبَاطِلِ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ تَكُوْنَ تِجَارَةً عَنْ تَرَاضٍ مِّنْكُمْ وَلَا تَقْتُلُوْۤا اَنْفُسَكُمْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ بِكُمْ رَحِيْمًا‏(29)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TAAKULOOA AMWAALAKUM BAYNAKUM BIL-BAATELE ILLAA AN TAKOONA TEJAARATAN A’N TARAAZIM MINKUM WA LAA TAQTULOOA FAQTOLOO INNAL LAAHA KAANA BEKUM RAHEEMAA.\nO’ ye believers! devour not each other’s property among yourselves unlawfully save that be trading by mutual consent; and kill not your (own) selves; Verily, God is Merciful unto you.\nوَمَنْ يَّفْعَلْ ذٰ لِكَ عُدْوَانًا وَّظُلْمًا فَسَوْفَ نُصْلِيْهِ نَارًا ؕ وَكَانَ ذٰ لِكَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ يَسِيْرًا‏(30)\nWA MAN MAN-Y ZAA LEKA U’UDWAANAN WWAZULMAN FA-SAWFA NUSLEEHE NAARAN KAANAL ZAA LEKA A’LAL LAAHE YASEERAA.\nAnd whoever shall do this in aggression and injustice, soon shall We cast him into the (Hell) fire; for this is (very) easy for God.\nاِنْ تَجْتَنِبُوْا كَبٰٓئِرَ مَا تُنْهَوْنَ عَنْهُ نُكَفِّرْ عَنْكُمْ سَيِّاٰتِكُمْ وَنُدْخِلْكُمْ مُّدْخَلًا كَرِيْمًا‏(31)\nIN TAJTANEBOOA KABAAAERA MAA TUNHAWNA A’NHO NUKAFFER A’NKUM SAYAAATEKUM WANUDKHELKUM MMUDKHALAN KAREEMAA.\nIf ye avoid the great sins which ye are forbidden, We will expiate from you (smaller) misdeeds, and We will admit you (to Paradise) an honourable (place of) entry (it is indeed).\nوَلَا تَتَمَنَّوْا مَا فَضَّلَ اللّٰهُ بِهٖ بَعْضَكُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ ؕ لِلرِّجَالِ نَصِيْبٌ مِّمَّا اكْتَسَبُوْا ؕ وَلِلنِّسَآءِ نَصِيْبٌ مِّمَّا اكْتَسَبْنَ ؕ وَسْئَلُوا اللّٰهَ مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمًا‏(32)\nWA LAA TATAMANNAWA MAA FAZZALA LAAHO BEHI BAA’ZAKUM A’LAA ELAA LELRREJAALE NASEEBUM MIMMAA MAKTASABOO WALELNNESAAE NASEEBUM MIMMAA AKTASABNA WASALOOA LAAHA MIN FAZLEHI INNAL LAAHA KAANA BEKULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEMAN.\nAnd covet not that by which God hath raised some of you above others; for men shall have of what they earn; and for women shall have of what they earn; and ask God of His Grace; Verily, God is (very well) in the Know of all things.\nوَلِكُلٍّ جَعَلْنَا مَوَالِىَ مِمَّا تَرَكَ الْوَالِدٰنِ وَالْاَقْرَبُوْنَ ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ عَقَدَتْ اَيْمَانُكُمْ فَاٰ تُوْهُمْ نَصِيْبَهُمْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ شَهِيْدًا ۙ‏(33)\nWA JA-A’LNAA MAWAALEAAA MIMMAA TARAKA AL-WAALEDAANE WAL AAQRABOONA WAL LAZEENA A’AQADAT AYMAANOKUM FA-AATOOHUNNA TOOHUM NASEEBAHUM INNAL LAAHA KAANA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN SHAHEEDAA.\nAnd to everyone We have appointed heirs (to inherit) of what (their) parents and near relatives have left behind; and (regarding) those with whom your right hands have made a covenant, give them their portion; Verily God is ever witness over all things.\nاَلرِّجَالُ قَوَّامُوْنَ عَلَى النِّسَآءِ بِمَا فَضَّلَ اللّٰهُ بَعْضَهُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ وَّبِمَاۤ اَنْفَقُوْا مِنْ اَمْوَالِهِمْ ؕ فَالصّٰلِحٰتُ قٰنِتٰتٌ حٰفِظٰتٌ لِّلْغَيْبِ بِمَا حَفِظَ اللّٰهُ ؕ وَالّٰتِىْ تَخَافُوْنَ نُشُوْزَهُنَّ فَعِظُوْهُنَّ وَاهْجُرُوْهُنَّ فِى الْمَضَاجِعِ وَاضْرِبُوْهُنَّ ۚ فَاِنْ اَطَعْنَكُمْ فَلَا تَبْغُوْا عَلَيْهِنَّ سَبِيْلًا ؕاِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ عَلِيًّا كَبِيْرًا‏(34)\nAALRREJAALU QAWAMOONA A’LAL NESAAA-E BEMAA FAZZALA LAAHO BA’ZAHUM A’LAA ELAA WWABEMAA ANFAQOO MIN AAMWAALEHEM FAALSSAALEHAATU QAANETAATUN HAAFEZAATUN LLELGHAYBE BEMAA HAFEZA LAAHO WA KHAALEKA TAKHAAFOONA NUSHOOZAHUNNA FAE’EZOOHUNNA WAAHJUROOHUNNA FIL AL-MAZAAJEE’E WAAZREBOOHUNNA FA-IN AATAA’NAKUM FALAA TABGHOOA A’LAYHINNA SABEELAA AENNA LAAHA KAANA A’ALEEA KABEERAA.\nMen have authority over women on account of the qualities with which God hath caused the one of them to excel the other and for what they spend of their property; therefore the righteous women are obedient, guarding the unseen that which God hath guarded; and as to those whose perverseness ye fear, admonish them and avoid them in beds and beat them; and if they obey you, then seek not a way against them; Verily, God is Ever-High, Ever- Great.\nوَاِنْ خِفْتُمْ شِقَاقَ بَيْنِهِمَا فَابْعَثُوْا حَكَمًا مِّنْ اَهْلِهٖ وَحَكَمًا مِّنْ اَهْلِهَا ۚ اِنْ يُّرِيْدَاۤ اِصْلَاحًا يُّوَفِّقِ اللّٰهُ بَيْنَهُمَا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ عَلِيْمًا خَبِيْرًا‏(35)\nWA KHIFTUM SHEQAAQA BAYNEHEMAA FAABA’ASOOA HAKAMAN MIN AHLEHI WAHAKAMAN MIN AHLEHAA IN YYUREEDAA WA YYOOFFEQE LAAHO BAYNAHOMAA INNAL LAAHA KAANA A’LEEMAN KHABEERAA.\nAnd if ye fear a breach between the couple, then send an arbitrator (chosen) from his family and an arbitrator (chosen) from her family; if they both desire compromise, God will affect harmony between the couple; Verily God is All Knowing, All-Aware.\nوَاعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ وَلَا تُشْرِكُوْا بِهٖ شَيْئًا ؕ وَّبِالْوَالِدَيْنِ اِحْسَانًا وَّبِذِى الْقُرْبٰى وَالْيَتٰمٰى وَ الْمَسٰكِيْنِ وَالْجَارِ ذِى الْقُرْبٰى وَالْجَارِ الْجُنُبِ وَالصَّاحِبِ بِالْجَنْۢبِ وَابْنِ السَّبِيْلِ ۙ وَمَا مَلَكَتْ اَيْمَانُكُمْ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُحِبُّ مَنْ كَانَ مُخْتَالًا فَخُوْرَا ۙ‏(36)\nWA BODUL LAAHA WA LAA TUSHREKOOA BEHI SHAY-ANW WWABEALWAALEDAYNE EHSAANANW WWABEZEAA QURBAA WAL YATAAMAA WA AL-MASAAKEENE WAL JAARE ZIL QURBAA WAL JAARE AL-JUNUBE WAALSSAAHEBE BIL-JANBE WAB SABEELE WA MAA MALAKAT AYMAANOKUM INNAL LAAHA LAA YOHIBBUL MAN KAANA MUKHTAALAN FAKHOORAA.\nWorships ye God (alone) and associate not aught with Him, and do good to parents, and to kinsfolk, and to orphans, and to the needy, and neighbour close to you and neighbour who is a stranger, and to a companion by your side and to the wayfarer, and to that which your right hands possess; Verily God loveth not the proud, the boastful.\nاۨلَّذِيْنَ يَبْخَلُوْنَ وَيَاْمُرُوْنَ النَّاسَ بِالْبُخْلِ وَيَكْتُمُوْنَ مَاۤ اٰتٰٮهُمُ اللّٰهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ ؕ وَ اَعْتَدْنَا لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ عَذَابًا مُّهِيْنًا ۚ‏(37)\nLAZEENA YABKHALOONA WAYAAMUROONA NAASA BIL-BUKHLE WA YAKTOMOONA MAA AAATAAHUMU LAAHO MIN FAZLEHI WA A-A’TADNAA LIL KAAFEREENA A’ZAABAN MOHEENAA.\nThose who are niggardly and bid people niggardliness, and hide away what God of His bounty hath given them; We have prepared for the disbelievers a torment ignominious.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يُنْفِقُوْنَ اَمْوَالَهُمْ رِئَآءَ النَّاسِ وَلَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَلَا بِالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِؕ وَمَنْ يَّكُنِ الشَّيْطٰنُ لَهٗ قَرِيْنًا فَسَآءَ قَرِيْنًا‏(38)\nWAL LAZEENA YUNFEQOONA AMWAALAHUM LAHU NAASE WA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL-LAAHE WA LAA BE-YAWME AAKHER WA MAN YYAKUNE SHAYTAANO LAHU QAREENAN FA-SAAA-A QAREENAN.\nAnd those who spend their property (in alms) to show to the people and believe not in God and in the Last Day (of Judgment); and he whose companion be Satan, (what) an evil companion then is he!\nوَمَاذَا عَلَيْهِمْ لَوْ اٰمَنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ وَاَنْفَقُوْا مِمَّا رَزَقَهُمُ اللّٰهُ ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ بِهِمْ عَلِيْمًا‏(39)\nWA MAA A’LAYHIM LAW AAMANOO BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE WA ANFAQOO MIMMAA RAZAQAHUMU LAAHO KAANAL LAAHO BEHIM A’LEEMAN.\nAnd what (harm) would it have done them if they had believed in God and the Last Day of (Judgment) and spent (benevolently) of what God hath provided them with; Verily God is (fully) aware of them.\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَظْلِمُ مِثْقَالَ ذَرَّةٍ ۚ وَاِنْ تَكُ حَسَنَةً يُّضٰعِفْهَا وَيُؤْتِ مِنْ لَّدُنْهُ اَجْرًا عَظِيْمًاؔ‏(40)\nINNAL LAAHA LAA YAZLEMU MISQAALA ZARRATIN WA TAKU HASANATANW YYUZAAE’EFHAA WAYUTE MIN LLADUNHU AJRAN A’AZEEMAN.\nVerily, God doth not injustice (even) to the weight of an atom, and if there be any good deed he multiplieth it and giveth of His own accord a great reward.\nفَكَيْفَ اِذَا جِئْنَا مِنْ كُلِّ اُمَّةٍ ۭ بِشَهِيْدٍ وَّجِئْنَا بِكَ عَلٰى هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ شَهِيْدًا ؕ‏(41)\nFA-KAYFA EZAA JENAA MIN KULLE UMMATIN BE-SHAHEED WWAJENAA BEKA A’LAA HAAOOLAAA-E SHAHEEDAA.\nHow will it be (then) when We shall bring forth from every people a witness and when We shall bring thee a witness over those (witnesses)?\nيَوْمَئِذٍ يَّوَدُّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَعَصَوُا الرَّسُوْلَ لَوْ تُسَوّٰى بِهِمُ الْاَرْضُ ؕ وَلَا يَكْتُمُوْنَ اللّٰهَ حَدِيْثًا‏(42)\nYAWMA-EZIN YYAWADDU LAZEENA KAFAROO WAA’ASAWUA YATTABE-U’R LAW TUSAWAA BEHEMUL ARZO WA LAA YAKTOMOONA LAAHA HADEESAN.\nOn that day will those who disbelieve and disobey the Prophet shall wish that the earth were levelled with them, But they shall not hide from God (even) a word.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَقْرَبُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاَنْتُمْ سُكَارٰى حَتّٰى تَعْلَمُوْا مَا تَقُوْلُوْنَ وَلَا جُنُبًا اِلَّا عَابِرِىْ سَبِيْلٍ حَتّٰى تَغْتَسِلُوْا ؕ وَاِنْ كُنْتُمْ مَّرْضٰۤى اَوْ عَلٰى سَفَرٍ اَوْ جَآءَ اَحَدٌ مِّنْكُمْ مِّنَ الْغَآئِطِ اَوْ لٰمَسْتُمُ النِّسَآءَ فَلَمْ تَجِدُوْا مَآءً فَتَيَمَّمُوْا صَعِيْدًا طَيِّبًا فَامْسَحُوْا بِوُجُوْهِكُمْ وَاَيْدِيْكُمْ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ عَفُوًّا غَفُوْرًا‏(43)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TAQRABOOA SALAATA WA ANTUM SUKAARAA HATTAA TA’LAMOO MAA TAQOOLOONA WA LAA JUNUBAN ILLAA A’AABEREAA SABEELIN HATTAA TAGHTASELOOA WA KUNTUM MARZAA AW A’LAA SAFARIN AW JAAA-A AHAD MINKUM MENAL AL-GHAAETE AW LAAMASTUMU NESAAA-A FALAM WA LAM MAAA-AN FATAYAMMAMOOA SAE’EEDAN TAYYEBAA FAAMSAHOOA BEWUJOOHEKUM WA AYDEEKUM INNAL LAAHA KAANA A’AFOOA GHAFOORAR.\nO’ ye who believe! approach not prayer when ye are intoxicated, until ye know (well) what ye say, nor when ye are polluted, unless ye be passing through, until ye wash yourself and if ye be sick, or on a journey, or one of you come from the privy or ye have touched the women and ye find not water then betake, yourself to clean (pure) earth and wipe (with it) a part of your faces and your hands; Verily God is Pardoning, Forgiving.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوْا نَصِيْبًا مِّنَ الْكِتٰبِ يَشْتَرُوْنَ الضَّلٰلَةَ وَيُرِيْدُوْنَ اَنْ تَضِلُّوا السَّبِيْلَ ؕ‏(44)\nALAM TARA ELAL LAZEENA OOTOO NASEEBAN MENAL KETAABE YASHTAROONA ZALAALATA WA YOREEDOONA AN TAZELLOOA SABEELA.\nHast thou not seen those to whom is given a part of the scripture? They buy error and wish that ye too go astray from the (right) way.\nوَاللّٰهُ اَعْلَمُ بِاَعْدَآئِكُمْؕ وَكَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ وَلِيًّا وَّكَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ نَصِيْرًا‏(45)\nWAL LAAHO A-A’LAMO BEAAA’DAAEKUM KAFAA BIL-LAAHE WALIYYANW WWAKAFAA BIL-LAAHE NASEERAA.\nBut God best knoweth your enemies; and suffices God as a protector and suffices God as a Helper.\nمِنَ الَّذِيْنَ هَادُوْا يُحَرِّفُوْنَ الْكَلِمَ عَنْ مَّوَاضِعِهٖ وَ يَقُوْلُوْنَ سَمِعْنَا وَعَصَيْنَا وَاسْمَعْ غَيْرَ مُسْمَعٍ وَّرَاعِنَا لَيًّۢا بِاَ لْسِنَتِهِمْ وَطَعْنًا فِىْ الدِّيْنِ ؕ وَلَوْ اَنَّهُمْ قَالُوْا سَمِعْنَا وَاَطَعْنَا وَاسْمَعْ وَانْظُرْنَا لَكَانَ خَيْرًا لَّهُمْ وَاَقْوَمَ ۙ وَ لٰكِنْ لَّعَنَهُمُ اللّٰهُ بِكُفْرِهِمْ فَلَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا‏(46)\nMENAL LAZEENA HAADOO YUHARREFOONA AL-KALEMA A’N MMAWAAZEE’EH WA YAQOOLOONA SAMEA’NAA WA WAASMAA’ GHAYRA MUSMAA’IN WWARAAE’ENAA LAYA BE-AFWAAHEKUM LSENATEHEM WATAA’NAN FEE DEENE WA LAW ANNAHUM QAALOO SAMEA’NAA WA ATA’NAA WAASMAA’ WA ZURNAA LAKAANA KHAYRAN LAHUM WAAQWAMA WA LAAKEN LA-A’NAHOMUL LAAHO BEKUFREHIM FALAA YOAMENOONA ILLAA QALEELAA.\nOf the Jews are those who (purposely) change the words from their places (to alter the meaning) and say “We have heard, and we have not obeyed,” and hear, but as one that heareth not and ‘‘Raina’ look at us, distorting (the word) with their tongues and taunting about the religion; But (instead) if they had said ‘We have heard, and we have obeyed, and (if they had said) ‘Isma’ (hearken) and ‘Unzurna’ (look at us) it were better for them, and more upright, but God hath cursed them for their disbelief, so they believe not, but only a few.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ اٰمِنُوْا بِمَا نَزَّلْنَا مُصَدِّقًا لِّمَا مَعَكُمْ مِّنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ نَّطْمِسَ وُجُوْهًا فَنَرُدَّهَا عَلٰٓى اَدْبَارِهَاۤ اَوْ نَلْعَنَهُمْ كَمَا لَعَنَّاۤ اَصْحٰبَ السَّبْتِؕ وَكَانَ اَمْرُ اللّٰهِ مَفْعُوْلًا‏(47)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA AAMENOO BEMAA NAZZALNAA MOSADDEQAL LEMAA MA-A’KUM MIN QABLE AN NNATMESA WUJOOHAN FANARUDDAHAA A’LAA AADBAAREHAA AW NALA’ANAHUM KAMAA LAA’ANNAA MASALAN AS-SABTE KAANAL AMRUL LAAHE MAF-O’OLAA.\nO’ ye, whom the Scripture hath been given! believe in what We have sent down confirming what is (already) with you, ere We change their faces (features) and turn them towards their backs, or as We cursed the people of Sabath; and (know ye, that) the Command of God is ever executed.\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَغْفِرُ اَنْ يُّشْرَكَ بِهٖ وَيَغْفِرُ مَا دُوْنَ ذٰ لِكَ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ ۚ وَمَنْ يُّشْرِكْ بِاللّٰهِ فَقَدِ افْتَرٰۤى اِثْمًا عَظِيْمًا‏(48)\nINNAL LAAHA LAA YAGHFERO AN YYUSHRAKA BEHI WA YAGHFERO MAA DOONA ZAA LEKA LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O WA MAN YYUSHREK BIL-LAAHE FAQADEH TARAA ISMAN A’ZEEMAA.\nVerily God for giveth not (anything) be associated with Him, but He forgiveth what is besides that whomsoever he pleaseth; and whoever associateth (aught) with God, hath indeed devised a great sin.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ يُزَكُّوْنَ اَنْفُسَهُمْ ؕ بَلِ اللّٰهُ يُزَكِّىْ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَلَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ فَتِيْلًا‏(49)\nALAM TARA ELAL LAZEENA YUZAKKOONA ANFOSAHUM BALIL LAAHO YUZAKKEAA MAN YASHAAA-O WA LAA LAA YUZLAMOON FATEELAN.\nHast thou not seen those who consider themselves pure? Nay: it is God who purifieth whomsoever He pleaseth, and they shall not be wronged (even) the husk of a date-stone.\nاُنْظُرْ كَيْفَ يَفْتَرُوْنَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ الْكَذِبَؕ وَكَفٰى بِهٖۤ اِثْمًا مُّبِيْنًا‏(50)\nAUNZUR KAYFA YAFTAROON A’LAL LAAHE AL-KAZEBA KAFAA BEHI ISMAN MOBEENAA.\nBehold how they forge a lie against God! and that (itself) is sufficient as a manifest sin.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوْا نَصِيْبًا مِّنَ الْكِتٰبِ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْجِبْتِ وَالطَّاغُوْتِ وَيَقُوْلُوْنَ لِلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا هٰٓؤُلَۤاءِ اَهْدٰى مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا سَبِيْلًا‏(51)\nALAM TARA ELAL LAZEENA OOTOO NASEEBAN MENAL KETAABE YOAMENOONA BIL-JEBTE WAALTTAAGHOOTE WA YAQOOLOONA LILLAZEENA KAFAROO HAAOOLAAA-E AHDAA MENAL LAZEENA AAMANOO SABEELAA.\nHast thou not observed those whom hath been given (a part) of the scripture? They believe in ‘Jibt ’ (idol) and ‘taghut’ (Satan) and say they about the infidels; “these are better guided in the path than those who believe (in God).\nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ لَعَنَهُمُ اللّٰهُ ؕ وَمَنْ يَّلْعَنِ اللّٰهُ فَلَنْ تَجِدَ لَهٗ نَصِيْرًا ؕ‏(52)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA LA-A’NAHOMUL LAAHO WA MAN YYALA’ANE LAAHO FALAN TAJEDA LAHU NASEERAA.\nThose are they whom God hath cursed; and whomsoever God curseth for him thou shalt not find any helper.\nاَمْ لَهُمْ نَصِيْبٌ مِّنَ الْمُلْكِ فَاِذًا لَّا يُؤْتُوْنَ النَّاسَ نَقِيْرًا ۙ‏(53)\nAM LAHUM NASEEBUM MENAL AL-MULKE FA EZAL LAA YOATOONAZ NAASA NAQEERAN.\nOr have they a share in the Kingdom (of the world)? But then they would not give to the people even the speck in the date-stone.\nاَمْ يَحْسُدُوْنَ النَّاسَ عَلٰى مَاۤ اٰتٰٮهُمُ اللّٰهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهٖۚ فَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَاۤ اٰلَ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ الْكِتٰبَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وَاٰتَيْنٰهُمْ مُّلْكًا عَظِيْمًا‏(54)\nAM YAHSUDOONA NAASA A’LAA MAA AAATAAHUMU LAAHO MIN FAZLEHI FAQAD AATAYNAA AALA IBRAAHEEMA KETAABA WAL HIKMATA WA AATAYNAAHUM MMULKAN A’ZEEMAA.\nOr do they envy the people for what God hath given them of His grace; But indeed We have given to Abraham’s children the Book and the Wisdom and We gave them a Great Kingdom.\nفَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ اٰمَنَ بِهٖ وَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ صَدَّ عَنْهُ ؕ وَكَفٰى بِجَهَنَّمَ سَعِيْرًا‏(55)\nFA-MINHUM MAN AAMANA BEHI WA MINHUM MAN SADDA A’NHO KAFAA YAWMAEZIM SA-E’ERAA.\nSo, of them is he who believeth on him (Muhammad) and of them is he who createth obstruction against him; and sufficient (to punish such) is the Burning Fire (of Hell).\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا سَوْفَ نُصْلِيْهِمْ نَارًا ؕ كُلَّمَا نَضِجَتْ جُلُوْدُهُمْ بَدَّلْنٰهُمْ جُلُوْدًا غَيْرَهَا لِيَذُوْقُوا الْعَذَابَ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ عَزِيْزًا حَكِيْمًا‏(56)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO BE-AAYAATENAA SAWFA NUSLEEHEM NAARAN KULLAMAA NAZEJAT JULOODUHUM BADDALNAAHUM JULOODAN GHAYRAHAA LEEZOOQOOA A’ZAABA INNAL LAAHA KAANA A’ZEEZAA HAKEEMAA.\nVerily (for) those who disbelieve Our signs, soon We will cast them into fire; so oft as their skins shall be burnt away, We will change for them other skins, that they may taste the torment; Verily God is Mighty, Wise!\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ سَنُدْخِلُهُمْ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَاۤ اَبَدًا ؕ لَهُمْ فِيْهَاۤ اَزْوَاجٌ مُّطَهَّرَةٌ  وَّنُدْخِلُهُمْ ظِلًّا ظَلِيْلًا‏(57)\nWAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE SANUDKHELUHUM JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ABADAM LAHUM FEEHAA AZWAAJUM MOTAHHARATUNW WWANUDKHELUHUM ZELLAN ZALEELAN.\nAnd (as for) those who believe and do good deeds We will admit them into gardens ‘neath which flow rivers, therein to abide for ever; therein shall be for them mates pure and We will make them to enter dense shades.\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَاْمُرُكُمْ اَنْ تُؤَدُّوا الْاَمٰنٰتِ اِلٰٓى اَهْلِهَا ۙ وَاِذَا حَكَمْتُمْ بَيْنَ النَّاسِ اَنْ تَحْكُمُوْا بِالْعَدْلِ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ نِعِمَّا يَعِظُكُمْ بِهٖ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ سَمِيْعًۢا بَصِيْرًا‏(58)\nINNAL LAAHA YAAMOROKUM AN TUADDOOA AL-AAMAANAATE ELAA AHLEHAA WA EZAA HAKAMTUM BAYNA NAASE AN TAHKUMOOA BIL-A’DL INNAL LAAHA NEE’EMMAA YA-E’ZOKUM BEHI INNAL LAAHA KAANA SAMEE-A’M BASEERAA.\nVerily God doth command you to render back your trusts to their owners, and when ye judge between men, to judge with justice; verily, how excellent is what God exhorteth you; Verily, God is the Hearer and the Seer.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اَطِيْعُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوا الرَّسُوْلَ وَاُولِى الْاَمْرِ مِنْكُمْۚ فَاِنْ تَنَازَعْتُمْ فِىْ شَىْءٍ فَرُدُّوْهُ اِلَى اللّٰهِ وَالرَّسُوْلِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ خَيْرٌ وَّاَحْسَنُ تَاْوِيْلًا‏(59)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO AATEEU’OOA LAAHA WAATEEU’OOA YATTABE-U’R WA ULIL AL-AAMRE MINKUM FA-IN TANAAZAA’TUM FEE SHAY-IN FARUDDOOHU ELAL LAAHE WA RASOOLE IN KUNTUM TUMENOONA BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE ZAA LEKA KHAYRUL WWAAHSANU TAAWEELAN.\nO’ ye who believe! obey God and obey the Apostle and those vested with authority from among you; and then if ye quarrel about anything refer it to God and the Apostle if ye believe in God and in the Last day (of Judgment)’, This is the best and the fairest way of ending (the dispute).\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ يَزْعُمُوْنَ اَنَّهُمْ اٰمَنُوْا بِمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكَ وَمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ مِنْ قَبْلِكَ يُرِيْدُوْنَ اَنْ يَّتَحَاكَمُوْۤا اِلَى الطَّاغُوْتِ وَقَدْ اُمِرُوْۤا اَنْ يَّكْفُرُوْا بِهٖ ؕ وَيُرِيْدُ الشَّيْطٰنُ اَنْ يُّضِلَّهُمْ ضَلٰلًاۢ بَعِيْدًا‏(60)\nALAM TARA ELAL LAZEENA YAZU’UMOONA ANNAHUM AAMANOO BEMAA UNZELA ELAYKA WA MAA UNZELA MIN QABLEKA YOREEDOONA AN YYATAHAAKAMOOA ELAL AT-TAAGHOOTE WA QAD MAAA OMEROO AN YYAKFUROOA BEHI WA YOREEDO SHAYTAANO AN YYUZELLAHUM ZALAALAM BAE’EEDAN.\nHast thou not observed those who think they believe in what hath been sent down unto thee and what hath been sent down before thee? they intend to resort to the judgment of ‘Taghoot ’ (the Satan) though commanded were they to abjure him; and Satan intendeth to mislead them far astray.\nوَاِذَا قِيْلَ لَهُمْ تَعَالَوْا اِلٰى مَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ وَاِلَى الرَّسُوْلِ رَاَيْتَ الْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ يَصُدُّوْنَ عَنْكَ صُدُوْدًا ۚ‏(61)\nWA EZAA QEELA LAHUM TA-A’ALAW ELAA MAA ANZALAL LAAHO WA ELAL RASOOLE RA-AYTA MONAAFEQEENA YASUDDOONA A’NKAL SUDOODAN.\nAnd when it is said unto them “Come (let us refer) to what God hath sent down (the Holy Qur’an) and to the Apostle (Muhammad)” thou seest the hypocrites turn away from thee with utter aversion.\nفَكَيْفَ اِذَاۤ اَصَابَتْهُمْ مُّصِيْبَةٌ ۢ بِمَا قَدَّمَتْ اَيْدِيْهِمْ ثُمَّ جَآءُوْكَ يَحْلِفُوْنَۖ بِاللّٰهِ اِنْ اَرَدْنَاۤ اِلَّاۤ اِحْسَانًا وَّتَوْفِيْقًا‏(62)\nFA-KAYFA EZAA ASAABATHUM MOSEEBATUN BEMAA QADDAMAT AYDEEHIM SUMMA JAAOOKA YAHLEFOONA BIL-LAAHE IN AARADNAA ILLAA EHSAANANW WWATAWFEEQAN.\nBut how then when some misfortune befalleth them on account of what their (own) hands have sent before (i.e. their own misdeeds), then will they come unto thee swearing by God (saying) “We desired not but (to promote) good and concord.\nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ يَعْلَمُ اللّٰهُ مَا فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ فَاَعْرِضْ عَنْهُمْ وَعِظْهُمْ وَقُلْ لَّهُمْ فِىْۤ اَنْفُسِهِمْ قَوْلًاۢ بَلِيْغًا‏(63)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA YA’LAMO LAAHO MAA FEE QOLOOBEHIM FAAA’REZ A’NHUM WAE’EZHUM WA QUL LAHUM FEE ANFOSEHIM QAWLAM BALEEGHAN.\nThese are those God knoweth what is (concealed) in their hearts, therefore turn aside from them, and admonish them and speak unto them concerning themselves words effectual.\nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا مِنْ رَّسُوْلٍ اِلَّا لِيُطَاعَ بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَلَوْ اَنَّهُمْ اِذْ ظَّلَمُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ جَآءُوْكَ فَاسْتَغْفَرُوا اللّٰهَ وَاسْتَغْفَرَ لَهُمُ الرَّسُوْلُ لَوَجَدُوا اللّٰهَ تَوَّابًا رَّحِيْمًا‏(64)\nWA MAA ARSALNAA MIN RASOOLIN ILLAA LEETAAA’A BE-IZNIL LAAHE WA LAW ANNAHUM IZ ZZALAMOOA ANFOSAHUM JAAOOKA FAASTAGHFAROOA LAAHA WAASTAGHFARA LAHOMUL RASOOLO LAWAJADOOA LAAHA TAWWAABAA RAHEEMAA.\nWe sent not an Apostle, but to be obeyed by God’s leave; And if they, when they were unjust to themselves (sinned), had only come unto thee and sought pardon of God and the Apostle (also) had asked pardon for them, surely would they have found God Oft-returning and the Most Merciful.\nفَلَا وَرَبِّكَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ حَتّٰى يُحَكِّمُوْكَ فِيْمَا شَجَرَ بَيْنَهُمْ ثُمَّ لَا يَجِدُوْا فِىْۤ اَنْفُسِهِمْ حَرَجًا مِّمَّا قَضَيْتَ وَيُسَلِّمُوْا تَسْلِيْمًا‏(65)\nFALAA WA RABBEKA LAA YOAMENOONA HATTAA YUHAKKEMOOKA FEEMAA SHAJARA BAYNAHUM SUMMA LAA YAJEDOOA FEE ANFOSEHIM HARAJAN MIMMAA QAZAYTA WAYUSALLEMOOA TASLEEMAA.\nSo, No! By thy Lord! they believe not (really) until they have set thee up their judge in all that they dispute about among themselves and thereafter find not in their selves any vexation (at all) against what thou decideth and submit (themselves) with total submission.\nوَلَوْ اَنَّا كَتَبْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ اَنِ اقْتُلُوْۤا اَنْفُسَكُمْ اَوِ اخْرُجُوْا مِنْ دِيَارِكُمْ مَّا فَعَلُوْهُ اِلَّا قَلِيْلٌ مِّنْهُمْ ؕ وَلَوْ اَنَّهُمْ فَعَلُوْا مَا يُوْعَظُوْنَ بِهٖ لَكَانَ خَيْرًا لَّهُمْ وَاَشَدَّ تَثْبِيْتًا ۙ‏(66)\nWA LAW ANNAA KATABNAA A’LAYHIM SAALEHAN AQTULOOA ANFOSAKUM AWE’ AKHRUJOOA MIN DEYAAREKUM MAA FAA’ALOOHU ILLAA QALEELUN MINHUM WA LAW ANNAHUM FAA’ALOOA MAA YOOA’AZOONA BEHI LAKAANA KHAYRAN LAHUM WA ASHADDA TASBEETAM.\nAnd (even) if We had prescribed for them saying “Kill yourselves or go forth from your dwellings, they would not have done it but a few of them; and if they had done what they were exhorted (to do), it would certainly have been better for them and more efficacious for strengthening (them in faith).\nوَّاِذًا لَّاٰتَيْنٰهُمْ مِّنْ لَّدُنَّاۤ اَجْرًا عَظِيْمًا ۙ‏(67)\nWWAAZAN LLAATAYNAAHUM MIN WA AJRAN A’ZEEMAA.\nAnd then We would certainly have given them of Our own accord a great recompense.\nوَّلَهَدَيْنٰهُمْ صِرَاطًا مُّسْتَقِيْمًا‏(68)\nWWALAHADAYNAAHUM SERAATAM MUSTAQEEMAA.\nAnd certainly would We have guided them on the straight path.\nوَمَنْ يُّطِعِ اللّٰهَ وَالرَّسُوْلَ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ مَعَ الَّذِيْنَ اَنْعَمَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِمْ مِّنَ النَّبِيّٖنَ وَالصِّدِّيْقِيْنَ وَالشُّهَدَآءِ وَالصّٰلِحِيْنَ ۚ وَحَسُنَ اُولٰٓئِكَ رَفِيْقًا ؕ‏(69)\nWA MAN YOTE-I’L LAAHA WA YATTABE-U’R FA-OOLAAA-EKA LAAHA LAZEENA AN-A’MAL LAAHO A’LAYHIM MENAL NABIYYEENA WAALSSEDDEEQEENA WA AN WA SAALEHEEN WAHASUNA OOLAAA-EKA RAFEEQAN.\nAnd whoever obeyeth God and the Apostle (Muhammad) these shall be with those, God hath bestowed favours upon them; of the Prophets, and the Truthful, and the Witnesses and the Righteous ones; and excellent are these as companions!\nذٰ لِكَ الْفَضْلُ مِنَ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَكَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ عَلِيْمًا‏(70)\nZAA LEKA FAZLUL MENAL LAAHE KAFAA BIL-LAAHE A’LEEMAN.\nThis is the grace from God; and sufficient is God (as the) Knower.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا خُذُوْا حِذْرَكُمْ فَانْفِرُوْا ثُبَاتٍ اَوِ انْفِرُوْا جَمِيْعًا‏(71)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO KHOZOO HEZRAKUM FAANFEROOA SUBAATIN AWE’ ANFEROOA JAMEE-A’A.\nO’ ye who believe! Take your precautions then sally forth in detachments or sally for all together (in a body).\nوَاِنَّ مِنْكُمْ لَمَنْ لَّيُبَطِّئَنَّۚ فَاِنْ اَصَابَتْكُمْ مُّصِيْبَةٌ قَالَ قَدْ اَنْعَمَ اللّٰهُ عَلَىَّ اِذْ لَمْ اَكُنْ مَّعَهُمْ شَهِيْدًا‏(72)\nWA INNA MINKUM LAMAN LLAYUBATTEANNA FA-IN AASAABATKUM MOSEEBATUN QAALA QAD AN-A’MAL LAAHO A’LAYYA IZ LAM AAKUN MMAA’AHUM SHAHEEDAA.\nAnd verily of you is he who certainly hangeth back! If then a misfortune befalleth you saith he “God had been gracious unto me, that I was not present with them.\nوَلَئِنْ اَصَابَكُمْ فَضْلٌ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ لَيَقُوْلَنَّ كَاَنْ لَّمْ تَكُنْۢ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَهٗ مَوَدَّةٌ يّٰلَيْتَنِىْ كُنْتُ مَعَهُمْ فَاَ فُوْزَ فَوْزًا عَظِيْمًا‏(73)\nWA LAIN AASAABAKUM FAZLUN MENAL LAAHE LAYAQOOLANNA KA-AN LAM TAKUN BAYNAKUM BAYNAHU MAWADDATUN YYAALAYTANEAA KUNTO MA-A’HUM FA-ALQEEHE FOOZA FAWZAN A’ZEEMAA.\nAnd if cometh unto you grace from God, he would certainly say as if there had not; been (an ties of) affection between you and him “Oh! would that I had been with them; a great achievement would I have achieved.\nفَلْيُقَاتِلْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ الَّذِيْنَ يَشْرُوْنَ الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَا بِالْاٰخِرَةِ ؕ وَمَنْ يُّقَاتِلْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ فَيُقْتَلْ اَوْ يَغْلِبْ فَسَوْفَ نُؤْتِيْهِ اَجْرًا عَظِيْمًا‏(74)\nFALYUQAATEL FEE SABEELIL LAAHE LAZEENA YASHROONA HAYAATAD DUNYAA BIL AAKHERATE WA MAN YYUQAATEL FEE SABEELIL LAAHE FAYUQTAL AW YAGHLEB FA-SAWFA NUTEEHE AJRAN A’ZEEMAA.\nLet those then fight in the way of God, who sell the life of this world for the hereafter; and to him who fighteth in the way of God, be he slain or (be he) victorious, We shall grant him a great recompense.\nوَمَا لَكُمْ لَا تُقَاتِلُوْنَ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَالْمُسْتَضْعَفِيْنَ مِنَ الرِّجَالِ وَالنِّسَآءِ وَالْوِلْدَانِ الَّذِيْنَ يَقُوْلُوْنَ رَبَّنَاۤ اَخْرِجْنَا مِنْ هٰذِهِ الْقَرْيَةِ الظَّالِمِ اَهْلُهَا ۚ وَاجْعَلْ لَّنَا مِنْ لَّدُنْكَ وَلِيًّا ۙۚ وَّاجْعَلْ لَّنَا مِنْ لَّدُنْكَ نَصِيْرًا ؕ‏(75)\nWA MAA LAKUM LAA TUQAATELOONA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WAL MUSTAZA’AFEENA MENAL AR-REJAALE WA NESAAA-E WAL WELDAANE LAZEENA YAQOOLOONA RABBANAA AAKHREJNAA MIN HAAZEHE QARYAH AZ-ZAALEME AAHLUHAA WA A’L LANAA MIN LLADUNKA WALIYYANW WWAAJA’AL LANAA MIN LLADUNKA NASEERAA.\nAnd what hath happened to you that ye fight not in the way of God and for the weak among men, women and children who (in helplessness) say, “O’ Our Lord! take us out of this town whose inhabitants are tyrants, and appoint for us from Thee a guardian and appoint for us from Thee a helper.\nاَلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا يُقَاتِلُوْنَ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ۚ وَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا يُقَاتِلُوْنَ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ الطَّاغُوْتِ فَقَاتِلُوْۤا اَوْلِيَآءَ الشَّيْطٰنِۚ اِنَّ كَيْدَ الشَّيْطٰنِ كَانَ ضَعِيْفًا‏(76)\nLAZEENA AAMANOO YOQAATELOONA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WAL LAZEENA KAFAROO YOQAATELOONA FEE SABEELIL AT-TAAGHOOTE FAQAATELOOA AAWLEEAAAA SHAYTAANE INNAL KAYDA SHAYTAANE KAANA HAQQO.\nThose who believe fight in the way of God and those who disbelieve fight in the way of Satan, fight therefore against the friends of Satan; Verily the craft of Satan is weak.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ قِيْلَ لَهُمْ كُفُّوْۤا اَيْدِيَكُمْ وَاَقِيْمُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاٰ تُوا الزَّكٰوةَ ۚ فَلَمَّا كُتِبَ عَلَيْهِمُ الْقِتَالُ اِذَا فَرِيْقٌ مِّنْهُمْ يَخْشَوْنَ النَّاسَ كَخَشْيَةِ اللّٰهِ اَوْ اَشَدَّ خَشْيَةً ۚ وَقَالُوْا رَبَّنَا لِمَ كَتَبْتَ عَلَيْنَا الْقِتَالَ ۚ لَوْلَاۤ اَخَّرْتَنَاۤ اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ قَرِيْبٍ ؕ قُلْ مَتَاعُ الدُّنْيَا قَلِيْلٌ ۚ وَالْاٰخِرَةُ خَيْرٌ لِّمَنِ اتَّقٰى وَلَا تُظْلَمُوْنَ فَتِيْلًا‏(77)\nALAM TARA ELAL LAZEENA QEELA LAHUM KUFFOOA AAYDEEKUM WA AQEEMUS SALAATA WAA TOOA ZAKAATA FALAMMAA KOTEBA A’LAYHEMUL QETAALO EZAA FAREEQUM MINHUM YAKHSHAWNA NAASA KA-KHASYATIL LAAHE AW ASHADDA KHASHYATAN WA QAALOO RABBANAA LEMA KATABTA A’LAYNAA QETAAL LAWLAA AAKKHARTANAA ELAA ELAA QAREEBIN QUL MATAAU’U DUNYAA QALEELUN WAL AAKHERATO KHAYRUL LLEMANE WAA WA LAA TUZLAMOON FATEELAN.\nHast thou not seen those unto whom was said “withhold your hand (from war) and establish prayer and pay the poor-rate,” but when fighting was prescribed for them, lo! a party of them fear men as (it should be) the fear of God, or even (with) a greater fear and say “O Our Lord! why hast Thou ordained upon us fighting, wherefore didst Thou not grant us respite to a near end;” Say (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) the provision of this world is scant and the hereafter is better for him who guardeth (himself against evil), and ye shall not be wronged (even to the extent of) the husk of a date-stone.\nاَيْنَ مَا تَكُوْنُوْا يُدْرِكْكُّمُ الْمَوْتُ وَلَوْ كُنْتُمْ فِىْ بُرُوْجٍ مُّشَيَّدَةٍ ؕ وَاِنْ تُصِبْهُمْ حَسَنَةٌ يَّقُوْلُوْا هٰذِهٖ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللّٰهِ ۚ وَاِنْ تُصِبْهُمْ سَيِّئَةٌ يَّقُوْلُوْا هٰذِهٖ مِنْ عِنْدِكَ ؕ قُلْ كُلٌّ مِّنْ عِنْدِ اللّٰهِ ؕ فَمَالِ ھٰٓؤُلَۤاءِ الْقَوْمِ لَا يَكَادُوْنَ يَفْقَهُوْنَ حَدِيْثًا‏(78)\nAYNA MAA TAKOONOO YUDREKKKUMU MAWTO WA LAW KUNTUM FEE BUROOJIN MMUSHAYDATIN WA IN TOSIBHUM HASANATUL YAQOOLOO HAAZEHI MIN I’NDIL LAAHE WA IN TOSIBHUM SAYYE-ATUM YAQOOLOO HAAZEHI MIN I’NDEK QUL KULLUL MIN I’NDIL LAAHE FAMAALE ULAAE QAWMIL LAA YAKAADOONA YAFQAHOON HADEESAN.\nWherever ye be, death will overtake you, even if ye be in towers (strong and) lofty; If good befalleth them they say, “This is from God” but if evil befalleth them say they “This is from thee;” Say (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) all is from God; But what hath happened to these people that well-nigh they understand not anything spoken (to them).\nمَاۤ اَصَابَكَ مِنْ حَسَنَةٍ فَمِنَ اللّٰهِ وَمَاۤ اَصَابَكَ مِنْ سَيِّئَةٍ فَمِنْ نَّفْسِكَ ؕ وَاَرْسَلْنٰكَ لِلنَّاسِ رَسُوْلًا ؕ وَكَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ شَهِيْدًا‏(79)\nMAA AASAABAKA MIN HASANATIN NAASE LAAHE WA MAA AASAABAKA MIN SAYATIN FAMIN NNAFSEKA WA ARSALNAAKA LIN-NAASE RASOOLAM KAFAA BIL-LAAHE SHAHEEDAA.\nWe have sent thee (Muhammad) as a Messenger unto Mankind and God is sufficient as Witness.\nمَنْ يُّطِعِ الرَّسُوْلَ فَقَدْ اَطَاعَ اللّٰهَ ۚ وَمَنْ تَوَلّٰى فَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنٰكَ عَلَيْهِمْ حَفِيْظًا ؕ‏(80)\nMAN YOTE-I’L YATTABE-U’R FAQAD AATAAA’A LAAHA WA MAN TAWALLAA FAMAA ARSALNAAKA A’LAYHIM HAFEEZAN.\nWhoso obeyeth the Apostle, he indeed obeyeth God; and whoever turneth away We have not sent thee upon them to watch.\nوَيَقُوْلُوْنَ طَاعَةٌ فَاِذَا بَرَزُوْا مِنْ عِنْدِكَ بَيَّتَ طَآئِفَةٌ مِّنْهُمْ غَيْرَ الَّذِىْ تَقُوْلُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَكْتُبُ مَا يُبَيِّتُوْنَ ۚ فَاَعْرِضْ عَنْهُمْ وَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى اللّٰهِ ؕ وَكَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ وَكِيْلًا‏(81)\nWA YAQOOLOONA TAAA’ATUN FA-EZAA BARAZOO MIN I’NDEK BAYTA TAAEFATUN MINHUM GHAYRA LAZEE TAQOOLO WAL LAAHO YAKTUBU MAA YUBAYTOONA FAAA’REZ A’NHUM WA TAWAKKAL A’LAL LAAHE KAFAA BIL-LAAHE WAKEELAA.\nAnd they say: ‘Obedience’, but when they get out from thy presence, a party of them brood by night over other than what thou sayest; and verily God writeth down what they brood by night, therefore turn aside from them and trust in God and God is sufficient Protector.\nاَفَلَا يَتَدَبَّرُوْنَ الْقُرْاٰنَؕ وَلَوْ كَانَ مِنْ عِنْدِ غَيْرِ اللّٰهِ لَوَجَدُوْا فِيْهِ اخْتِلَافًا كَثِيْرًا‏(82)\nAFALAA YATADABBAROONA QURAAN WA LAW KAANA MIN I’NDIL GHAIRE LAAHE LAWAJADOOA FEEHE AKHTELAAFAN KASEERAA.\nDo they not think (carefully) in Qur’an? And if it had been from any other than God, they would surely have found in it much discrepancy.\nوَاِذَا جَآءَهُمْ اَمْرٌ مِّنَ الْاَمْنِ اَوِ الْخَوْفِ اَذَاعُوْا بِهٖ ۚ وَلَوْ رَدُّوْهُ اِلَى الرَّسُوْلِ وَاِلٰٓى اُولِى الْاَمْرِ مِنْهُمْ لَعَلِمَهُ الَّذِيْنَ يَسْتَنْۢبِطُوْنَهٗ مِنْهُمْؕ وَلَوْلَا فَضْلُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَتُهٗ لَاتَّبَعْتُمُ الشَّيْطٰنَ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا‏(83)\nWA EZAA JAAA-AHUM AAMRUN MENAL AL-AAMNE AWE’ KHAWFE AAZAAU’OOA BEHI WA LAW RADDOOHU ELAL RASOOLE WA ELAA ULIL AL-AAMRE MINHUM LAA’ALEMAHU LAZEENA YASTANBETOONAH MENHUM WA LAWLAA FAZLUL LAAHE A’LAYKUM WA RAHMATOHU LAATTABAA’TUMU ASH-SHAYTAANA ILLAA QALEELAA.\nAnd when there cometh unto them news of security or (of) alarm, they spread it abroad; and if they had referred it to the Apostle and (to) those in authority from among them, (who could) draw the matter (the truth) in it; would have known it (the truth) from them; and were it not for the grace of God upon you and His mercy, you would certainly have followed the devil save a few.\nفَقَاتِلْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ۚ لَا تُكَلَّفُ اِلَّا نَفْسَكَ وَحَرِّضِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ ۚ عَسَے اللّٰهُ اَنْ يَّكُفَّ بَاْسَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ اَشَدُّ بَاْسًا وَّاَشَدُّ تَنْكِيْلًا‏(84)\nFAQAATEL FEE SABEELIL LAAHE LAA TOKALLAFO ILLAA NAFSAKA WAHARREZE MOAMENEEN A’ASA LAAHO AN YYAKUFFA BAASA LAZEENA KAFAROO WAL LAAHO ASHADDO BAASAN WWAASHADDU TANKEELAN.\nFight then in God’s way: it is not imposed (on any) except in relation to thyself; and stir up the faithful, may be God will restrain the might of those who disbelieve, Verily, God is the strongest in might and the severest in punishing.\nمَنْ يَّشْفَعْ شَفَاعَةً حَسَنَةً يَّكُنْ لَّهٗ نَصِيْبٌ مِّنْهَا ۚ وَمَنْ يَّشْفَعْ شَفَاعَةً سَيِّئَةً يَّكُنْ لَّهٗ كِفْلٌ مِّنْهَا ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ مُّقِيْتًا‏(85)\nMAN YYASHFAA’ SHAFAAA’ATAN HASANATANW YYAKUN LAHU NASEEBUM MINHAA WA MAN YYASHFAA’ SHAFAAA’ATAN SAYYE-ATANW YYAKUN LAHU KEFLUN MINHAA KAANAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN MMUQEETAN.\nWhoever intercedeth with a good intercession shall have a share therefrom; and whoever intercedeth a bad intercession shall bear the burden of it; and God keepeth control over all things.\nوَاِذَا حُيِّيْتُمْ بِتَحِيَّةٍ فَحَيُّوْا بِاَحْسَنَ مِنْهَاۤ اَوْ رُدُّوْهَا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ حَسِيْبًا‏(86)\nWA EZAA HUYYEETUM BETAHEETIN FAHAYWA BE-AHSANAL MINHAA AW RUDDOOHAA INNAL LAAHA KAANA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN HASEEBAA.\nWhen ye are greeted with a greeting, then greet ye with a better (than it), or return it; Verily, God, of all things, taketh account.\nاللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَؕ لَيَجْمَعَنَّكُمْ اِلٰى يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ لَا رَيْبَ فِيْهِؕ وَمَنْ اَصْدَقُ مِنَ اللّٰهِ حَدِيْثًا‏(87)\nLAAHO LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOO LAYAJMAA’ANNAKUM ELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE LAA RAYBA FEEH WA MAN AASDAQU MENAL LAAHE HADEESAN.\nGod! there is no God but He! He will certainly gather you all together on the Day of Resurrection; there is no doubt in it; who can be more True in Word than God?\nفَمَا لَكُمْ فِىْ الْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ فِئَتَيْنِ وَاللّٰهُ اَرْكَسَهُمْ بِمَا كَسَبُوْاؕ اَ تُرِيْدُوْنَ اَنْ تَهْدُوْا مَنْ اَضَلَّ اللّٰهُ ؕ وَمَنْ يُّضْلِلِ اللّٰهُ فَلَنْ تَجِدَ لَهٗ سَبِيْلًا‏(88)\nFAMAA LAKUM FEE MONAAFEQEENA FEATAYNE WAL LAAHO AARKASAHUM BEMAA KASABOOA A’ZAABAN TOREEDOONA AN TAHDOOA MAN AZALLAL LAAHO WA MAN YYUZLELE LAAHO FALAN TAJEDA LAHU SABEELAA.\nWhat hath happened to you (that) ye are two parties about the hypocrites? Verily, God hath reversed them for what they have earned; intend ye to guide those whom God hath forsaken to stray? For those whom God hath forsaken to stray, never shall thou find a way.\nوَدُّوْا لَوْ تَكْفُرُوْنَ كَمَا كَفَرُوْا فَتَكُوْنُوْنَ سَوَآءً فَلَا تَتَّخِذُوْا مِنْهُمْ اَوْلِيَآءَ حَتّٰى يُهَاجِرُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ؕ فَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَخُذُوْهُمْ وَاقْتُلُوْهُمْ حَيْثُ وَجَدتُّمُوْهُمْ وَلَا تَتَّخِذُوْا مِنْهُمْ وَلِيًّا وَّلَا نَصِيْرًا ۙ‏(89)\nWADDOOA LAW TAKFOROONA KAMAA KAFAROO FATAKOONOONA SAWAAAN FALAA TATTAKHEZOOA MINHUM AAWLEEAAAA HATTAA YUHAAJEROOA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE FA-IN TAWALLAW FAKHUZOOHUM WAQ TOLOOHUM HAYSO WAJADTTUMOOHUM WA LAA TATTAKHEZOOA MINHUM WALIYYANW WA LAA NASEERAA.\nThey long that ye should be infidels as they are infidels, so that ye may be (all) alike, therefore take not friends from among them until they migrate in God’s way; But if they turn back, then seize them and slay them wherever ye find them, and take none of them as friends, and as helpers.\nاِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ يَصِلُوْنَ اِلٰى قَوْمٍۢ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَهُمْ مِّيْثَاقٌ اَوْ جَآءُوْكُمْ حَصِرَتْ صُدُوْرُهُمْ اَنْ يُّقَاتِلُوْكُمْ اَوْ يُقَاتِلُوْا قَوْمَهُمْ ؕ وَلَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ لَسَلَّطَهُمْ عَلَيْكُمْ فَلَقٰتَلُوْكُمْ ۚ فَاِنِ اعْتَزَلُوْكُمْ فَلَمْ يُقَاتِلُوْكُمْ وَاَلْقَوْا اِلَيْكُمُ السَّلَمَ ۙ فَمَا جَعَلَ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ عَلَيْهِمْ سَبِيْلًا‏(90)\nILLAA LAZEENA YASELOONA ELAA QAWMIN BAYNAKUM WA BAYNAHUM MMEESAAQUN AW JAAA-OOKUM HASERAT SODOOROHUM AN YYUQAATELOOKUM AW YUQAATELOOA QAWMAHUM WA LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO LASALLATAHUM A’LAYKUM FALAQAATALOOKUM FA-ENIN AA’TAZALOOKUM FALAM YUQAATELOOKUM WAALQAWA AELAYKUMU AS-SALAMA FAMAA JA-A’LA LAAHO LAKUM A’LAYHIM SABEELAA.\nExcept those who reach a people between whom and yon is a covenant (of peace) or who come unto you, (with) their hearts restraining them from fighting you; or fighting their own people; and if God had pleased, He would have given them power over you, so certainly they would have fought you; therefore, if they withdraw from you and do not fight you, and surrender, then God hath made no way for you (to fight) against them.\nسَتَجِدُوْنَ اٰخَرِيْنَ يُرِيْدُوْنَ اَنْ يَّاْمَنُوْكُمْ وَيَاْمَنُوْا قَوْمَهُمْ ؕ كُلَّمَا رُدُّوْۤا اِلَى الْفِتْنَةِ اُرْكِسُوْا فِيْهَا ۚ فَاِنْ لَّمْ يَعْتَزِلُوْكُمْ وَيُلْقُوْۤا اِلَيْكُمُ السَّلَمَ وَيَكُفُّوْۤا اَيْدِيَهُمْ فَخُذُوْهُمْ وَاقْتُلُوْهُمْ حَيْثُ ثَقِفْتُمُوْهُمْ ؕ وَاُولٰٓئِكُمْ جَعَلْنَا لَكُمْ عَلَيْهِمْ سُلْطٰنًا مُّبِيْنًا‏(91)\nSATAJEDOONA AAKHEREEN YOREEDOONA AN YYAAMANOOKUM WAYAAMANOOA QAWMAHUM KULLAMAA RUDDOOA ELAL AL-FETNATE AURKESOOA FEEHAA FA-IN LAM YAA’TAZELOOKUM WAYULQOOA AELAYKUMU AS-SALAMA WAYAKUFFOOA AYDEYAHUM FAKHUZOOHUM WAQ TOLOOHUM HAYSO SAQIFTOMOOHUM WAAWLAAAEKUM JA-A’LNAA LAKUM A’LAYHIM SULTAANAN MOBEENAA.\nShortly: ye will find others who desire security from you and security from their own people; Every time they are returned to mischief, they plunge into it headlong; Therefore if they withdraw not from you and surrender (not) seeking peace and nor restrain their hands, then seize them and slay them wherever ye find them; and (it is) against these of you We have given you a clear authority.\nوَمَا كَانَ لِمُؤْمِنٍ اَنْ يَّقْتُلَ مُؤْمِنًا اِلَّا خَطَئًا ۚ وَمَنْ قَتَلَ مُؤْمِنًا خَطَئًا فَتَحْرِيْرُ رَقَبَةٍ مُّؤْمِنَةٍ وَّدِيَةٌ مُّسَلَّمَةٌ اِلٰٓى اَهْلِهٖۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّصَّدَّقُوْا ؕ فَاِنْ كَانَ مِنْ قَوْمٍ عَدُوٍّ لَّكُمْ وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ فَتَحْرِيْرُ رَقَبَةٍ مُّؤْمِنَةٍ ؕ وَاِنْ كَانَ مِنْ قَوْمٍۢ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَهُمْ مِّيْثَاقٌ فَدِيَةٌ مُّسَلَّمَةٌ اِلٰٓى اَهْلِهٖ وَ تَحْرِيْرُ رَقَبَةٍ مُّؤْمِنَةٍ ۚ فَمَنْ لَّمْ يَجِدْ فَصِيَامُ شَهْرَيْنِ مُتَتَابِعَيْنِ تَوْبَةً مِّنَ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ عَلِيْمًا حَكِيْمًا‏(92)\nWA MAA KAANA LE-MOAMENINW AN YYAQTULA MUMENAN ILLAA KHATAAN WA MAN QATALA MUMENAN KHATAAN FATAHREERU RAQABATIN MMUMENATIN WWADEETUN MMUSALLAMATUN ELAA AHLEHI ILLAA AN YYASSADDAQOOA FA-IN KAANA MIN QAWMIN A’ADOO LAKUM WA HOWA MUMENUN FATAHREERU RAQABATIN MMUMENATIN WA KAANA MIN QAWMIN BAYNAKUM WA BAYNAHUM MMEESAAQUN FADEETUN MMUSALLAMATUN ELAA AHLEHI WA TAHREERU RAQABATIN MMUMENATIN FAMAN LAM YAJID FA-SEYAAMO SHAHRAYNE MUTATAABEA’AYNE TAWBATAN MENAL LAAHE KAANAL LAAHO A’LEEMAN HAKEEMAA.\nA believer killeth not a believer except (it happens) by mistake and whoso killeth a believer by mischance, should (set) free a believer-slave and blood-money should be paid to his people unless they remit it as alms; but if he be from a tribe hostile unto you and he be a believer, the freeing of a believer slave (suffices); and if he be from a tribe between whom and you there is a covenant, the blood money should be paid to his people along with the freeing of a believer-slave; but he who findeth not (means) to do this, should fast for two months consecutively (as) a penance from God; and God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.\nوَمَنْ يَّقْتُلْ مُؤْمِنًا مُّتَعَمِّدًا فَجَزَآؤُهٗ جَهَنَّمُ خَالِدًا فِيْهَا وَغَضِبَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَلَعَنَهٗ وَاَعَدَّ لَهٗ عَذَابًا عَظِيْمًا‏(93)\nWA MAN YYAQTUL MUMENAN MMUTAA’AMMEDAN FAJAZAAUH JAHANNAMUL KHAALEDAN FEEHAA WA GHAZEBAL LAAHO A’LAYHE WALAA’ANAH WA A-A’DDA LAHU A’ZAABAN A’ZEEMAA.\nAnd whosoever killeth a believer intentionally, his recompense shall be Hell, he shall abide therein and God’s wrath shall be on him and His curse, and (there) is prepared for him a great torment.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِذَا ضَرَبْتُمْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ فَتَبَيَّنُوْا وَلَا تَقُوْلُوْا لِمَنْ اَ لْقٰٓى اِلَيْكُمُ السَّلٰمَ لَسْتَ مُؤْمِنًا ۚ تَبْتَغُوْنَ عَرَضَ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا فَعِنْدَ اللّٰهِ مَغَانِمُ كَثِيْرَةٌ ؕ كَذٰلِكَ كُنْتُمْ مِّنْ قَبْلُ فَمَنَّ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْكُمْ فَتَبَيَّنُوْا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ خَبِيْرًا‏(94)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO EZAA ZARABTUM FEE SABEELIL LAAHE FATABAYNOOA WA LAA TAQOOLOO LEMAN-Y A’ZAABAN LQAAA AELAYKUMU AS-SALAAMA LASTA MUMENAN TABTAGHOONA A’ARAZA HAYAATID DUNYAA FA I’NDAL LAAHE MAGHAANEMU KASEERATUN KAZAALEKA KUNTUM MIN QABLO FAMANNA LAAHO A’LAYKUM FATABAYNOOA INNAL LAAHA KAANA BEMAA TA’MALOON KHABEERAA.\nO’ ye who believe! when ye march forth (to fight) in the way of God discriminate ye (carefully) discern, and say ye not to anyone who offereth you salutation (peace) “thou art not a believer;” coveting the chance goods of (this) worldly life (whereas) with God are plenteous gains; Even thus, (as he is now) were ye (yourselves) before, but God conferred (His) grace on you; therefore discern ye (carefully); Verily God is All-Aware of what (all) ye do.\nلَا يَسْتَوِى الْقَاعِدُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ غَيْرُ اُولِى الضَّرَرِ وَالْمُجَاهِدُوْنَ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ بِاَمْوَالِهِمْ وَاَنْفُسِهِمْ ؕ فَضَّلَ اللّٰهُ الْمُجٰهِدِيْنَ بِاَمْوَالِهِمْ وَاَنْفُسِهِمْ عَلَى الْقٰعِدِيْنَ دَرَجَةً  ؕ وَكُلًّا وَّعَدَ اللّٰهُ الْحُسْنٰىؕ وَفَضَّلَ اللّٰهُ الْمُجٰهِدِيْنَ عَلَى الْقٰعِدِيْنَ اَجْرًا عَظِيْمًا ۙ‏(95)\nLAA YASTAWEAA AL-QAAE’EDOONA MENAL MOAMENEEN GHAYRO ULIL AZ-ZARARE WAL MUJAAHEDOONA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE BEAAMWAALEHEM WA ANFOSEHIM FAZZALA LAAHO AL-MUJAAHEDEENA BEAAMWAALEHEM WA ANFOSEHIM A’LAL AL-QAAE’EDEENA DARAJATAN WAKULLAN WWAA’ADA LAAHO HUSNAA WAFAZZALA LAAHO AL-MUJAAHEDEENA A’LAL AL-QAAE’EDEENA AJRAN A’ZEEMAA.\nNot equal are those of the believers who sit (holding hack) other than those hurt, and those who strive in the way of God with their wealth and their selves (lives); God hath raised the strivers with their wealth and selves (lives), in rank above those sit ting (holding back); Unto all (in faith) God hath promised good; but those who strive, He hath distinguished above those who sit (holding back) (by) a great recompense.\nدَرَجٰتٍ مِّنْهُ وَمَغْفِرَةً وَّرَحْمَةً ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ غَفُوْرًا رَّحِيْمًا‏(96)\nDARAJAATIN MINHO WAMAGHFERATAN WA RAHMATAL KAANAL LAAHO GHAFOORAR RAHEEMAA.\nRanks (High) (assigned) by Him and pardon and Mercy; for God is Oft-Forgiving, All- Merciful.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ تَوَفّٰٮهُمُ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ ظَالِمِىْۤ اَنْفُسِهِمْ قَالُوْا فِيْمَ كُنْتُمْؕ قَالُوْا كُنَّا مُسْتَضْعَفِيْنَ فِىْ الْاَرْضِؕ قَالُوْۤا اَلَمْ تَكُنْ اَرْضُ اللّٰهِ وَاسِعَةً فَتُهَاجِرُوْا فِيْهَاؕ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ مَاْوٰٮهُمْ جَهَنَّمُؕ وَسَآءَتْ مَصِيْرًا ۙ‏(97)\nINNAL LAZEENA TAWAFFAAHUMU TAHMELOHUL ZAALEMEAA ANFOSEHIM QAALOO FEEMA KUNTUM QAALOO KUNNAA MUSTAZA’AFEENA FEE ARZ QAALOO ALAM TAKUN AARZU LAAHE WAASEA’ATAN FATUHAAJEROOA FEEHAA FA-OOLAAA-EKA MAAWAAHUM JAHANNAM WA WA SAA-AT MASEERAA.\nVerily those whom the angels take away (at death) while they are unjust to their (own) selves (in sin), they (the angels) shall ask (the sinner souls) “In what state were ye?” They shah reply “Weakened (and oppressed) were we in the land;” They (angels) will say “Was not the land of God vast (enough) for you to migrate therein?” So these (are those) whose refuge shall be Hell; and what a bad resort it is.\nاِلَّا الْمُسْتَضْعَفِيْنَ مِنَ الرِّجَالِ وَالنِّسَآءِ وَالْوِلْدَانِ لَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ حِيْلَةً وَّلَا يَهْتَدُوْنَ سَبِيْلًا ۙ‏(98)\nILLAA AL-MUSTAZA’AFEENA MENAL AR-REJAALE WA NESAAA-E WAL WELDAANE LAA YASTATEE-O’ONA HEELATAN WA LAA YAHTADOON SABEELAA.\nExcept the (really) weakened ones from among the men and the women and the children, who have not in their power the means (to escape from the unbelievers) and nor they find the (right) way.\nفَاُولٰٓئِكَ عَسَى اللّٰهُ اَنْ يَّعْفُوَ عَنْهُمْؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ عَفُوًّا غَفُوْرًا‏(99)\nFA-OOLAAA-EKA A’ASAA LAAHO AN YYAA’FOO A’ANHUM KAANAL LAAHO A’AFOOA GHAFOORAR.\nSo these, may be, God will pardon them; and God is the Clement, the Oft-Forgiving.\nوَمَنْ يُّهَاجِرْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ يَجِدْ فِى الْاَرْضِ مُرٰغَمًا كَثِيْرًا وَّسَعَةً ؕ وَمَنْ يَّخْرُجْ مِنْۢ بَيْتِهٖ مُهَاجِرًا اِلَى اللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖ ثُمَّ يُدْرِكْهُ الْمَوْتُ فَقَدْ وَقَعَ اَجْرُهٗ عَلَى اللّٰهِ ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ غَفُوْرًا رَّحِيْمًا‏(100)\nWA MAN YYUHAAJER FEE SABEELIL LAAHE YAJID FIL ARZE MURAAGHAMAN KASEERAA WWASAA’ATAN WA MAN YYAKHRUJ MIN BAYTEH MUHAAJERAN ELAL LAAHE WA RASOOLEHI SUMMA YUDREKHU MAWTO FAQAD WAQA-A’L AJROHU A’LAL LAAHE KAANAL LAAHO GHAFOORAR RAHEEMAA.\nAnd whosoever migrateth in the way of God, findeth in the earth refuge abundant and spacious; and whoever goeth forth from his house migrating unto God and His Apostle (Muhammad), and then (before he reacheth the destination) death overtaketh him, indeed hath become his recompense incumbent upon God; and God is Oft-Forgiving, Merciful.\nوَاِذَا ضَرَبْتُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ فَلَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ جُنَاحٌ اَنْ تَقْصُرُوْا مِنَ الصَّلٰوةِ ۖ اِنْ خِفْتُمْ اَنْ يَّفْتِنَكُمُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا ؕ اِنَّ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ كَانُوْا لَكُمْ عَدُوًّا مُّبِيْنًا‏(101)\nWA EZAA ZARABTUM FIL ARZE FA-LAYSA A’LAYKUM JONAAHUN AN TAQSUROOA MENAL AS-SALAAWTE IN KHIFTUM AN YYAFTENAKUMU LAZEENA KAFAROO INNAL KAAFEREEN KAANOO LAKUM A’DUWWAL MOBEENAA.\nWhen ye travel in the earth, it shall be no blame on you if ye shorten the prayers if ye fear that those who disbelieve will cause you distress. Verily, the infidels to you are open enemies.\nوَاِذَا كُنْتَ فِيْهِمْ فَاَقَمْتَ لَهُمُ الصَّلٰوةَ فَلْتَقُمْ طَآئِفَةٌ مِّنْهُمْ مَّعَكَ وَلْيَاْخُذُوْۤا اَسْلِحَتَهُمْ فَاِذَا سَجَدُوْا فَلْيَكُوْنُوْا مِنْ وَّرَآئِكُمْ وَلْتَاْتِ طَآئِفَةٌ اُخْرٰى لَمْ يُصَلُّوْا فَلْيُصَلُّوْا مَعَكَ وَلْيَاْخُذُوْا حِذْرَهُمْ وَاَسْلِحَتَهُمْ ۚ وَدَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَوْ تَغْفُلُوْنَ عَنْ اَسْلِحَتِكُمْ وَاَمْتِعَتِكُمْ فَيَمِيْلُوْنَ عَلَيْكُمْ مَّيْلَةً وَّاحِدَةً ؕ وَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكُمْ اِنْ كَانَ بِكُمْ اَ ذًى مِّنْ مَّطَرٍ اَوْ كُنْتُمْ مَّرْضٰۤى اَنْ تَضَعُوْۤا اَسْلِحَتَكُمْ ۚ وَ خُذُوْا حِذْرَكُمْ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ اَعَدَّ لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ عَذَابًا مُّهِيْنًا‏(102)\nWA EZAA KUNTA FEEHIM FAAQAMTA LAHOMUL SALAATA FALTAQUM TAAEFATUN MINHUM BEMAM WALYAAKHUZOOA AASLEHATAHUM FA-EZAA SAJADOOA FALYAKOONOOA MIN WWARAAEKUM WALTAATE TAAEFATUN LAHU LAM YUSALLOOA FALYUSALLOOA MA-A’KA WALYAAKHUZOOA HEZRAHUM WAASLEHATAHUM WADDA LAZEENA KAFAROO LAW TAGHFULOONA A’N AASLEHATEKUM WAAMTEA’ATEKUM FAYAMEELOONA A’LAYKUM MMAYLATAN WAAHEDATAN WA LAA JONAAHA A’LAYKUM IN KAANA BEKUM A’ZAABAN ZAN MIN MMATARIN AW KUNTUM MARZAA AN TAZAU’OOA AASLEHATAKUM WA KHOZOO HEZRAKUM INNAL LAAHA A-A’DDA LIL KAAFEREENA A’ZAABAN MOHEENAA.\nWhen thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) art among them (when a battle rages) and thou establishest prayer for them, then let a party of them stand up with thee and let them take their arms; then when they have prostrated (themselves) let them take their position in your rear, and let the other party come up, which hath not prayed, then let them pray with thee, but let them take their precautions and their arms; for, desire those who disbelieve that if ye be negligent of your arms and your baggages, that they may turn upon you all at once; But it shall be no blame on you, if ye be inconvenienced by rain or be ill that ye put away your arms; but take your precaution; Verily God hath prepared for the infidels, a disgraceful torment.\nفَاِذَا قَضَيْتُمُ الصَّلٰوةَ فَاذْكُرُوا اللّٰهَ قِيَامًا وَّقُعُوْدًا وَّعَلٰى جُنُوْبِكُمْ ۚؕ فَاِذَا اطْمَاْنَنْتُمْ فَاَقِيْمُوا الصَّلٰوةَ ۚ اِنَّ الصَّلٰوةَ كَانَتْ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ كِتٰبًا مَّوْقُوْتًا‏(103)\nFA-EZAA QAZAYTUMU SALAATA FAZKORUL LAAHA QEEAMAN WWAQUU’OODAN WWAA’ALAA JUNOOBEKUM FA-EZAA ATMAANANTUM FAAQEEMOOA SALAATA INNAL SALAATA KAANAT A’LAL MOAMENEEN KETAABAA MMAWQOOTAN.\nAnd when ye have finished the prayer remember God standing, and sitting, and reclining, and when ye are secure (from danger), establish prayer; Verily Prayer is, (imposed) upon the believers as (a) timed Ordinance.\nوَلَا تَهِنُوْا فِى ابْتِغَآءِ الْقَوْمِ ؕ اِنْ تَكُوْنُوْا تَاْلَمُوْنَ فَاِنَّهُمْ يَاْلَمُوْنَ كَمَا تَاْلَمُوْنَ ۚ وَتَرْجُوْنَ مِنَ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا يَرْجُوْنَ ؕ وَ كَانَ اللّٰهُ عَلِيْمًا حَكِيْمًا‏(104)\nWA LAA TAHENOOA FIL ABTEGHAAE QAWMIL IN TAKOONOO TAALAMOONA FA INNAHUM YAALAMOONA KAMAA TAALAMOONA WATARJOONA MENAL LAAHE MAA LAA YARJOON WA KAANA LAAHO A’LEEMAN HAKEEMAA.\nAnd slacken not in pursuit of the (enemy) people; If ye suffer pain, assuredly they also suffer as ye suffer; but ye hope from God what they hope not; And God is All-Knowing and All-Wise.\nاِنَّاۤ اَنْزَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ الْكِتٰبَ بِالْحَقِّ لِتَحْكُمَ بَيْنَ النَّاسِ بِمَاۤ اَرٰٮكَ اللّٰهُ ؕ وَلَا تَكُنْ لِّلْخَآئِنِيْنَ خَصِيْمًا ۙ‏(105)\nINNAA ANZALNAA ELAYKA KETAABA BIL-HAQQE LETAHKUMA BAYNA NAASE BEMAA AARAAKA LAAHO WA LAA TAKUN LLELKHAAENEENA KHASEEMAN.\nVerily We have sent down unto thee the Book (The Qur’an) with the Truth that thou mayest judge between people by what God showeth thee; and be not thou a pleader for the treacherous.\nوَّاسْتَغْفِرِ اللّٰهَ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ غَفُوْرًا رَّحِيْمًا ۚ‏(106)\nWWAASTAGHFERE LAAHA INNAL LAAHA KAANA GHAFOORAR RAHEEMAA.\nAnd pray for the Pardon of God (for thy followers), Verily, God is Oft-Forgiving, Merciful.\nوَلَا تُجَادِلْ عَنِ الَّذِيْنَ يَخْتَانُوْنَ اَنْفُسَهُمْ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُحِبُّ مَنْ كَانَ خَوَّانًا اَثِيْمًا ۙ ۚ‏(107)\nWA LAA TUJAADEL A’NIL LAZEENA YAKHTAANOONA ANFOSAHUM INNAL LAAHA LAA YOHIBBUL MAN KAANA KHAWANAN AASEEMAN.\nAnd plead not on behalf of those who deceive their own selves; Verily God loveth not any who is treacherous, sinful.\nيَّسْتَخْفُوْنَ مِنَ النَّاسِ وَلَا يَسْتَخْفُوْنَ مِنَ اللّٰهِ وَهُوَ مَعَهُمْ اِذْ يُبَيِّتُوْنَ مَا لَا يَرْضٰى مِنَ الْقَوْلِؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ بِمَا يَعْمَلُوْنَ مُحِيْطًا‏(108)\nYYASTAKHFOONA MENAL NAASE WA LAA YASTAKHFOONA MENAL LAAHE WA HOWA MA-A’HUM IZ YUBAYTOONA MAA LAA YARZAA MENAL AL-QAWLE KAANAL LAAHO BEMAA YA’MALOON MUHEETAN.\nThey hide from people but they hide not from God and He is with them when they hold nightly discourses which He is not pleased with; And God doth compass round what all they do.\nهٰۤاَنْتُمْ هٰٓؤُلَۤاءِ جَادَلْتُمْ عَنْهُمْ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا فَمَنْ يُّجَادِلُ اللّٰهَ عَنْهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ اَمْ مَّنْ يَّكُوْنُ عَلَيْهِمْ وَكِيْلًا‏(109)\nHAANTUM HAAOOLAAA-E JAADALTUM A’NHUM FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA FAMAN YYUJAADELU LAAHA A’NHUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE AM MAN YYAKOONU A’LAYHIM WAKEELAA.\nBehold! ye pleaded for these in this worldly life; hut who shall plead with God for them on the Day of Resurrection? or who shall be their defender?\nوَ مَنْ يَّعْمَلْ سُوْٓءًا اَوْ يَظْلِمْ نَفْسَهٗ ثُمَّ يَسْتَغْفِرِ اللّٰهَ يَجِدِ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرًا رَّحِيْمًا‏(110)\nWA MAN YA’MAL SOOO-AN AW YAZLEM NAFSAH SUMMA YASTAGHFERE LAAHA YAJEDE LAAHA GHAFOORAR RAHEEMAA.\nAnd whoever doth evil, or wrongeth his own self and thereafter seeketh pardon of God, shall find God Oft-Forgiving, Merciful.\nوَمَنْ يَّكْسِبْ اِثْمًا فَاِنَّمَا يَكْسِبُهٗ عَلٰى نَفْسِهٖؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ عَلِيْمًا حَكِيْمًا‏(111)\nWA MAN YYAKSEB ISMAN FA-INNAMAA YAKSEBUH A’LAA NAFSEH KAANAL LAAHO A’LEEMAN HAKEEMAA.\nWhoever comitteth a sin, verily, he committeth it against his own self; And God is All Knowing, All-Wise.\nوَمَنْ يَّكْسِبْ خَطِيْٓئَةً اَوْ اِثْمًا ثُمَّ يَرْمِ بِهٖ بَرِيْٓئًا فَقَدِ احْتَمَلَ بُهْتَانًا وَّاِثْمًا مُّبِيْنًا‏(112)\nWA MAN YYAKSEB KHATEEATAN AW ISMAN SUMMA YARME BEHI BAREEAN FAQADEH AHTAMALA BOHTAANANW WA ISMAM MOBEENAA.\nAnd whoever committeth a fault or a sin and throweth it on one innocent he indeed burdeneth (himself) with the calumny and a manifest sin.\nوَلَوْلَا فَضْلُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكَ وَرَحْمَتُهٗ لَهَمَّتْ طَّآئِفَةٌ مِّنْهُمْ اَنْ يُّضِلُّوْكَ ؕ وَمَا يُضِلُّوْنَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْفُسَهُمْ وَمَا يَضُرُّوْنَكَ مِنْ شَىْءٍ ؕ وَاَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْكَ الْكِتٰبَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وَعَلَّمَكَ مَا لَمْ تَكُنْ تَعْلَمُؕ وَكَانَ فَضْلُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكَ عَظِيْمًا‏(113)\nWA LAWLAA FAZLUL LAAHE A’LAYKA WA RAHMATOHU LAHAMMAT TAAA-EFATUM MINHUM AN YYUZELLOOKA WA MAA YUZELLOONA ILLAA ANFOSAHUM WA MAA YAZURROONAKA MIN SHAY-IN WA ANZALA LAAHO A’LAYKA KETAABA WAL HIKMATA WAA’ALLAMAKA MAA LAM TAKUN TAA’LAMU KAANAL FAZLUL LAAHE A’LAYKA A’ZEEMAA.\nHad it not been God’s grace upon thee and His mercy, a party among them had certainly resolved to lead thee astray; but they shall not lead thee astray but their own selves, and they shall, not harm thee of aught; and God hath sent down unto thee the Book and Wisdom, and hath taught thee what thou didst not know; and God’s grace on thee is very great.\nلَا خَيْرَ فِىْ كَثِيْرٍ مِّنْ نَّجْوٰٮهُمْ اِلَّا مَنْ اَمَرَ بِصَدَقَةٍ اَوْ مَعْرُوْفٍ اَوْ اِصْلَاحٍۢ بَيْنَ النَّاسِ ؕ وَمَن يَّفْعَلْ ذٰ لِكَ ابْتِغَآءَ مَرْضَاتِ اللّٰهِ فَسَوْفَ نُؤْتِيْهِ اَجْرًا عَظِيْمًا‏(114)\nLAA KHAYRAZ FEE KASEERIM MIN NNAJWAAHUM ILLAA MAN AMARAL BE-SADAQATIN AW MAA’ROOFIN AW AESLAAHIN BAYNA NAASE WAMAN MAN-Y ZAA LEKA TEGHAAA-A MARZAATIL LAAHE FA-SAWFA NUTEEHE AJRAN A’ZEEMAA.\nThere is nothing good in most of their whisperings except (in his) who bideth charity or goodness or peace among the people; And whoever doth this seeking the pleasure of God, anon We will give him a great recompense.\nوَمَنْ يُّشَاقِقِ الرَّسُوْلَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُ الْهُدٰى وَ يَتَّبِعْ غَيْرَ سَبِيْلِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ نُوَلِّهٖ مَا تَوَلّٰى وَنُصْلِهٖ جَهَنَّمَ ؕ وَسَآءَتْ مَصِيْرًا‏(115)\nWA MAN YYUSHAAQEQE YATTABE-U’R MIN BA’DE MAA TABAYYANA LAHUL HODAA WA YATTABEA’ GHAYRA SABEELIL MOAMENEEN NOOLLEH MAA TAWALLAA WANUSLEH JAHANNAMA WA SAA-AT MASEERAA.\nAnd whosoever opposeth the Apostle (Muhammad) after that guidance hath been manifest to him and followeth a way other than that of the believers, We will turn him to that to which he hath (himself) turned and will cast him into Hell; and Oh! what a bad destination it is!\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَغْفِرُ اَنْ يُّشْرَكَ بِهٖ وَيَغْفِرُ مَا دُوْنَ ذٰ لِكَ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَمَنْ يُّشْرِكْ بِاللّٰهِ فَقَدْ ضَلَّ ضَلٰلًاۢ بَعِيْدًا‏(116)\nINNAL LAAHA LAA YAGHFERO AN YYUSHRAKA BEHI WA YAGHFERO MAA DOONA ZAA LEKA LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O WA MAN YYUSHREK BIL-LAAHE FAQAD ZALLA ZALAALAM BAE’EEDAN.\nVerily God forgiveth not that (anything) be associated with Him, and forgiveth anything besides this to whomsoever He pleaseth; and whoso associated! (aught) with God, hath indeed strayed far, far away (from the right path).\nاِنْ يَّدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اِلَّاۤ اِنٰثًا ۚ وَاِنْ يَّدْعُوْنَ اِلَّا شَيْطٰنًا مَّرِيْدًا ۙ‏(117)\nIN YAD-O’ONA MIN DOONEHI ILLAA AENAASAN WA YAD-O’ONA ILLAA SHAYTAANAN MMAREEDAN.\nThey (The Pagans) invoke not besides Him but the female deities (the Idols) and they invoke not but Satan the persistent rebel (void of all good).\nلَّعَنَهُ اللّٰهُ ۘ وَقَالَ لَاَ تَّخِذَنَّ مِنْ عِبَادِكَ نَصِيْبًا مَّفْرُوْضًا ۙ‏(118)\nLLAA’ANAHU LAAHO WA QAALA LAA TTAKHEZANNA MIN E’BAADEKAS NASEEBAN MMAFROOZAN.\nWhom God hath cursed him and he (the Satan) said “Most certainly will I take of Thy bondsmen an allotted share.\nوَّلَاُضِلَّنَّهُمْ وَلَاُمَنِّيَنَّهُمْ وَلَاٰمُرَنَّهُمْ فَلَيُبَتِّكُنَّ اٰذَانَ الْاَنْعَامِ وَلَاٰمُرَنَّهُمْ فَلَيُغَيِّرُنَّ خَلْقَ اللّٰهِؕ وَمَنْ يَّتَّخِذِ الشَّيْطٰنَ وَلِيًّا مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ فَقَدْ خَسِرَ خُسْرَانًا مُّبِيْنًا ؕ‏(119)\nWWALAAZELLANNAHUM WALAAMANNEENNAHUM WALAAMURANNAHUM FALAYUBATTEKUNNA AAAZAANA AL-AANA’AAME WALAAMURANNAHUM FALAYUGHAYRUNNA KHALQA LAAH WA MAN YYATTAKHEZE ASH-SHAYTAANA WALIYYANW MIN DOONIL LAAHE FAQAD KHASERA KHUSRAANAN MOBEENAA.\nAnd assuredly will I lead them astray and certainly stir (vain) desires in them, and certainly bid them that they slit the ears of cattle, and will I certainly command them that they shall change (the faces) of God’s creation;” And whoever taketh Satan as a guardian besides God, indeed suffereth he a manifest loss.\nيَعِدُهُمْ وَيُمَنِّيْهِمْ ؕ وَمَا يَعِدُهُمُ الشَّيْطٰنُ اِلَّا غُرُوْرًا‏(120)\nYAE’EDUHUM WAYUMANNEEHEM WA MAA YAE’EDUHUMU SHAYTAANO ILLAA GHOROORAA.\nHe (Satan) giveth them (false) promises and (he) stirreth (vain) desires in them; but Satan promiseth not (aught) but (it is sheer) deception.\nاُولٰٓئِكَ مَاْوٰٮهُمْ جَهَنَّمُ وَلَا يَجِدُوْنَ عَنْهَا مَحِيْصًا‏(121)\nOOLAAA-EKA MAAWAAHUM JAHANNAMUL WA LAA YAJEDOONA A’NHAA MAHEESAN.\nThese, (Satan’s dupes), their abode shall be Hell, and they shall not find from it any escape.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ سَنُدْخِلُهُمْ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَاۤ اَبَدًا ؕ وَعْدَ اللّٰهِ حَقًّا ؕ وَمَنْ اَصْدَقُ مِنَ اللّٰهِ قِيْلًا‏(122)\nWAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE SANUDKHELUHUM JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ABADAM WA’DAL LAAHE HAQQAN WA MAN AASDAQU MENAL LAAHE QEELAN.\nBut they who believe and do righteous deeds, shortly We will admit them into gardens ‘neath which flow rivers, for ever shall they abide therein; (It is) a promise of God. (It is) true indeed; And who can be more true than God in utterance.\nلَيْسَ بِاَمَانِيِّكُمْ وَلَاۤ اَمَانِىِّ اَهْلِ الْكِتٰبِؕ مَنْ يَّعْمَلْ سُوْٓءًا يُّجْزَ بِهٖۙ وَ لَا يَجِدْ لَهٗ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَلِيًّا وَّلَا نَصِيْرًا‏(123)\nLAYSA BEAAMAANEEKUM WA LAA AAMAANEAAAE AHLIL AL-KETAABE MAN YA’MAL SOOO-AN YYUJZA BEHI WA LAA YAJID LAHU MIN DOONIL LAAHE WALIYYANW WA LAA NASEERAA.\n(It shall) not be according to your desires nor the desires of the people of the Book; (but) whoever doeth evil shall be recompensed for it, nor will he find for himself, besides God, any guardian or a helper.\nوَمَنْ يَّعْمَلْ مِنَ الصّٰلِحٰتِ مِنْ ذَكَرٍ اَوْ اُنْثٰى وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ يَدْخُلُوْنَ الْجَنَّةَ وَلَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ نَقِيْرًا‏(124)\nWA MAN YA’MAL MENAL SAALEHAATE MIN ZAKARIN AW UNSAA WA HOWA MUMENUN FA-OOLAAA-EKA YADKHOLOONA JANNATA WA LAA LAA YUZLAMOON NAQEERAN.\nAnd whoso doeth deeds of righteousness, whether male or female, and be a believer, then these shall enter Heaven and they shall not be wronged (even) to the husk of a date-stone.\nوَمَنْ اَحْسَنُ دِيْنًا مِّمَّنْ اَسْلَمَ وَجْهَهٗ لِلّٰهِ وَهُوَ مُحْسِنٌ وَّاتَّبَعَ مِلَّةَ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ حَنِيْفًا ؕ وَاتَّخَذَ اللّٰهُ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ خَلِيْلًا‏(125)\nWA MAN AHSANO DEENAN MIMMAYN ASLAMA WAJHAHU LILLAAHE WA HOWA MOHSENUN WWAATTABAA’A MILLATA IBRAAHEEMA HANEEFAA WA TAKHAZA LAAHO IBRAAHEEMA KHALEELAN.\nAnd who is better in religion than he who resigneth himself entirely unto God? and is righteous, and followeth the creed of Abraham, the Upright One, And God took Abraham for a Friend.\nوَلِلّٰهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ مُّحِيْطًا‏(126)\nLILLAAHE MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZ KAANAL LAAHO BEKULLE SHAY-IN MMUHEETAN.\nTo God belongeth whatever is in the heavens and all that is in the earth; and God encompasseth all things.\nوَيَسْتَفْتُوْنَكَ فِى النِّسَآءِ ؕ قُلِ اللّٰهُ يُفْتِيْكُمْ فِيْهِنَّ ۙ وَمَا يُتْلٰى عَلَيْكُمْ فِى الْكِتٰبِ فِىْ يَتٰمَى النِّسَآءِ الّٰتِىْ لَا تُؤْتُوْنَهُنَّ مَا كُتِبَ لَهُنَّ وَتَرْغَبُوْنَ اَنْ تَنْكِحُوْهُنَّ وَالْمُسْتَضْعَفِيْنَ مِنَ الْوِلْدَانِ ۙ وَاَنْ تَقُوْمُوْا لِلْيَتٰمٰى بِالْقِسْطِ ؕ وَمَا تَفْعَلُوْا مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ بِهٖ عَلِيْمًا‏(127)\nWAYASTAFTOONAKA FIL NESAAA-E QOLIL LAAHO YUFTEEKUM FEEHINNA WA MAA YUTLAA A’LAYKUM FIL KETAABE FEE YATAAMAA NESAAA-E KHAALEKA LAA TUTOONAHUNNA MAA KOTEBA LAHUNNA WATARGHABOONA AN TANKEHOOHUNNA WAL MUSTAZA’AFEENA MENAL AL-WELDAANE WA TAQOOMOOA LIL-YATAAMAA BIL QISTE WA MAA TAF-A’LOO MIN KHAYRIN FA-INNAL LAAHA KAANA BEHI A’LEEMAN.\nThey ask thee for a decision about women Say! (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “God doth decision for you about them; and that which is recited unto you in the book concerning orphan girls, whom ye give not what is assigned to them, while (yet) ye desire to wed them, and also (concerning) the Weak among the children, that ye stand firm tor the orphans, with justice; and whatever of good ye do. Verily God knoweth it.\nوَاِنِ امْرَاَةٌ خَافَتْ مِنْۢ بَعْلِهَا نُشُوْزًا اَوْ اِعْرَاضًا فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْهِمَاۤ اَنْ يُّصْلِحَا بَيْنَهُمَا صُلْحًا ؕ وَالصُّلْحُ خَيْرٌ ؕ وَاُحْضِرَتِ الْاَنْفُسُ الشُّحَّ ؕ وَاِنْ تُحْسِنُوْا وَتَتَّقُوْا فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ خَبِيْرًا‏(128)\nWA ENIS AMRAATUN KHAAFAT MIN BAA’LEHAA NUSHOOZAN AW AEA’RAAZAN FALAA JONAAHA FEEMAF AN YYUSLEHAA BAYNAHOMAA SULHAN WAALSSULHU KHAYRUL WAAHZERATE AL-AANFUSU ASH-SHUHHA WA TUHSENOOA WA TATTAQOO FA-INNAL LAAHA KAANA BEMAA TA’MALOON KHABEERAA.\nAnd if a woman feareth ill-treatment desertion from her husband, then shall it be no fault on the twain if they effect compromise (peace) between them two amicably; for compromise (peace) is good; and Avarice is made to be present in (people’s) minds; and if ye do good and guard yourselves (against evil ), then verily God is All-Aware of what ye do.\nوَلَنْ تَسْتَطِيْعُوْۤا اَنْ تَعْدِلُوْا بَيْنَ النِّسَآءِ وَلَوْ حَرَصْتُمْ فَلَا تَمِيْلُوْا كُلَّ الْمَيْلِ فَتَذَرُوْهَا كَالْمُعَلَّقَةِ ؕ وَاِنْ تُصْلِحُوْا وَتَتَّقُوْا فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ غَفُوْرًا رَّحِيْمًا‏(129)\nWA LAN TASTATEEU’OOA AN TAA’DELOOA BAYNA NESAAA-E WA LAW HARASTUM FALAA TAMEELOOA KULLA AL-MAYLE FATAZAROOHAA KAALMUA’ALLAQATE WA TUSLEHOOA WA TATTAQOO FA-INNAL LAAHA KAANA GHAFOORAR RAHEEMAA.\nYe will not be able to deal equally between (your) wives, however much ye wish (to do so). But turn not altogether away (from one), leaving her as in suspense. If ye do good and keep from evil, Verily, God is Ever-Forgiving, Merciful.\nوَاِنْ يَّتَفَرَّقَا يُغْنِ اللّٰهُ كُلًّا مِّنْ سَعَتِهٖ ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ وَاسِعًا حَكِيْمًا‏(130)\nWA YYATAFARRAQAA YUGHNE LAAHO KULLAN MIN SAA’ATEH KAANAL LAAHO WAASEA’AN HAKEEMAA.\nAnd if they separate, God will render (e)each free from want out of His abundance; and God is Omniscient, Wise.\nوَلِلّٰهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ ؕ وَلَقَدْ وَصَّيْنَا الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ وَاِيَّاكُمْ اَنِ اتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ ؕ وَاِنْ تَكْفُرُوْا فَاِنَّ لِلّٰهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ غَنِيًّا حَمِيْدًا‏(131)\nLILLAAHE MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE WA LAQAD WASSAYNAA LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA MIN QABLEKUM WA IYYAAKUM SAALEHAN TAQUL LAAHA WA TAKFUROOA FA-INNAL LILLAAHE MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZ KAANAL LAAHO GHANEEA HAMEEDAN.\nAnd God’s is whatever is in the heavens and whatever is in the earth; and indeed We enjoined those who were given the Book before you, and unto you (too) that ye should take shelter in God; and if ye disbelieve, then, verily, God’s is whatever is m the heavens and whatever is in the earth; God is Self-Sufficient, Praise-worthy.\nوَلِلّٰهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ ؕ وَكَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ وَكِيْلًا‏(132)\nLILLAAHE MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE KAFAA BIL-LAAHE WAKEELAA.\nAnd God’s is whatever is in the heavens and whatever is in the earth; and God is sufficient as a Protector.\nاِنْ يَّشَاْ يُذْهِبْكُمْ اَيُّهَا النَّاسُ وَيَاْتِ بِاٰخَرِيْنَؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى ذٰلِكَ قَدِيْرًا‏(133)\nIN YYASHAA YUZHEBKUM AYYOHAL NAASO WA TAKOONOO BEAAAKHAREENA KAANAL LAAHO A’LAA ZAALEKA QADEERAA.\nIf He pleaseth, He can cause you pass away, O’ people! and bring others (in your stead); and for this God hath power.\nمَنْ كَانَ يُرِيْدُ ثَوَابَ الدُّنْيَا فَعِنْدَ اللّٰهِ ثَوَابُ الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ سَمِيْعًاۢ بَصِيْرًا‏(134)\nMAN KAANA YOREEDO SAWAABA DUNYAA FA I’NDAL LAAHE SAWAABUL DUNYAA WAL AAKHERAH KAANAL LAAHO SAMEE-A’M BASEERAA.\nWhoever desireth the reward of this world, then with God is the reward of this world and the hereafter; and God is All-Hearing and All-Seeing.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا كُوْنُوْا قَوَّامِيْنَ بِالْقِسْطِ شُهَدَآءَ لِلّٰهِ وَلَوْ عَلٰٓى اَنْفُسِكُمْ اَوِ الْوَالِدَيْنِ وَالْاَقْرَبِيْنَ ؕ اِنْ يَّكُنْ غَنِيًّا اَوْ فَقِيْرًا فَاللّٰهُ اَوْلٰى بِهِمَا فَلَا تَتَّبِعُوا الْهَوٰٓى اَنْ تَعْدِلُوْا ۚ وَاِنْ تَلْوٗۤا اَوْ تُعْرِضُوْا فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ خَبِيْرًا‏(135)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO KOONOO QAWAMEENA BIL QISTE SHOHADAAA-A LILLAAHE WA LAW A’LAA ANFOSEKUM AWE’ AL-WAALEDAYNE WAL AQRABEENA IN YYAKUN GHANEEA AW FAQEERAN FAL-LAAHO AAWLAA BEHEMAA FALAA TATTABEU’OOA AL-HAWAA AN TAA’DELOOA WA TALWA AW TUA’REZOOA FA-INNAL LAAHA KAANA BEMAA TA’MALOON KHABEERAA.\nO’ ye who believe! do stand firmly with justice, Witnesses for God’s sake, though it be against your own selves or your parents or your kindred, be he rich or poor, for God is closer (than you) to them both; Therefore follow not your inclination, lest ye deviate, (from the truth) and if ye swerve (from the truth) or turn aside, then Verily God is All-A ware of what ye do.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اٰمِنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖ وَالْكِتٰبِ الَّذِىْ نَزَّلَ عَلٰى رَسُوْلِهٖ وَالْكِتٰبِ الَّذِىْۤ اَنْزَلَ مِنْ قَبْلُؕ وَمَنْ يَّكْفُرْ بِاللّٰهِ وَمَلٰٓئِكَتِهٖ وَكُتُبِهٖ وَرُسُلِهٖ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ فَقَدْ ضَلَّ ضَلٰلًاۢ بَعِيْدًا‏(136)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO AAMENOO BIL-LAAHE WA RASOOLEHI WAL KETAABE LAZEE NAZZALAL A’LAA RASOOLEHI WAL KETAABE LAZEE ANZALAL MIN QABL WA WA MAN YAKFUR BIL-LAAHE WA MALAA-EKATEHI WA KOTOBEHI WA ROSOLEHI WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE FAQAD ZALLA ZALAALAM BAE’EEDAN.\nO’ ye who believe! Believe in God, and His Apostle and the Book which He hath sent down unto His Apostle (Muhammad) and the Book which He hath sent down before (him); and whoever denieth God, and His Angels, and His Books, and His Apostles and the Last Day (of judgment) hath indeed strayed off, far away (from the right path).\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا ثُمَّ كَفَرُوْا ثُمَّ اٰمَنُوْا ثُمَّ كَفَرُوْا ثُمَّ ازْدَادُوْا كُفْرًا لَّمْ يَكُنِ اللّٰهُ لِيَغْفِرَ لَهُمْ وَلَا لِيَهْدِيَهُمْ سَبِيْلًا ؕ‏(137)\nINNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO SUMMA KAFAROO SUMMA AAMANOO SUMMA KAFAROO SUMMA AZDAADOOA KUFRAN LAM YAKONIL LAAHO LEEGHFERA LAHUM WA LAA LEEHDEEHUM SABEELAA.\nVerily, those who believed and thereafter disbelieved, again believed, and again disbelieved, thereafter increased they in disbelief, It is not for God to pardon them, nor will He guide them to the (right) way.\nبَشِّرِ الْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ بِاَنَّ لَهُمْ عَذَابًا اَلِيْمًاۙ‏(138)\nBASH-SHERIL MONAAFEQEENA BE-ANNAL LAHUM A’ZAABAN ALEEMAA.\nAnnounce (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) to the hypocrites that for them there shall be a painful torment.\nۨالَّذِيْنَ يَتَّخِذُوْنَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ اَوْلِيَآءَ مِنْ دُوْنِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ ؕ اَيَبْتَغُوْنَ عِنْدَهُمُ الْعِزَّةَ فَاِنَّ الْعِزَّةَ لِلّٰهِ جَمِيْعًا ؕ‏(139)\nLAZEENA YATTAKHEZOONA KAAFEREEN AAWLEEAAAA MIN DOONIL MOAMENEEN AAYABTAGHOONA E’ENDAHUMU AL-E’EZZATA FA-INNAL AL-E’EZZATA LILLAAHE JAMEE-A’A.\nThose who take the disbelievers for (their) friends rather than believers; Do they seek honour from them? Then, Verily, All honour (as a whole) belongeth (only) to God.\nوَقَدْ نَزَّلَ عَلَيْكُمْ فِى الْكِتٰبِ اَنْ اِذَا سَمِعْتُمْ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ يُكْفَرُ بِهَا وَيُسْتَهْزَاُبِهَا فَلَا تَقْعُدُوْا مَعَهُمْ حَتّٰى يَخُوْضُوْا فِىْ حَدِيْثٍ غَيْرِهٖۤ  ۖ اِنَّكُمْ اِذًا مِّثْلُهُمْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ جَامِعُالْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ وَالْكٰفِرِيْنَ فِىْ جَهَنَّمَ جَمِيْعَاۨ ۙ‏(140)\nWA QAD NAZZALAL A’LAYKUM FIL KETAABE AN EZAA SAMEA’TUM AAYAATIL LAAHE YUKFARU BEHAA WAYUSTAHZAABEHAA FALAA TAQU’UDOOA MA-A’HUM HATTAA YAKHOOZOOA FEE HADEESIN GHAYREH INNAKUM EZAL MMESLUHUM INNAL LAAHA JAAMEU’UALMUNAAFEQEENA WA KAAFEREEN FEE JAHANNAMA JAMEEA’AA.\nAnd indeed hath He sent down unto you (O’ Believers!) in the Book (Qur’an) that when ye hear the signs of God disbelieved in, and mocked at, then sit ye not with them until they enter into some other discourse, otherwise, ye would become like them; Verily, God will gather the hypocrites and the infidels in Hell all together.\nالَّذِيْنَ يَتَرَ بَّصُوْنَ بِكُمْ ۚ فَاِنْ كَانَ لَكُمْ فَتْحٌ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ قَالُوْۤا اَلَمْ نَكُنْ مَّعَكُمْ  ۖ وَاِنْ كَانَ لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ نَصِيْبٌۙ قَالُوْۤا اَلَمْ نَسْتَحْوِذْ عَلَيْكُمْ وَنَمْنَعْكُمْ مِّنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ ؕ فَاللّٰهُ يَحْكُمُ بَيْنَكُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ ؕ وَلَنْ يَّجْعَلَ اللّٰهُ لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ سَبِيْلًا‏(141)\nLAZEENA MOTALLAQAATO BBASOONA BEKUM FA-IN KAANA LAKUM FATHUN MENAL LAAHE QAALOO ALAM NAKUN MMAA’AKUM WA KAANA LIL KAAFEREENA NASEEBUM QAALOO ALAM NASTAHWEZ A’LAYKUM WANAMNAA’KUM MENAL MOAMENEEN FAL-LAAHO YAHKOMO BAYNAKUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE WA LAN YYAJA’ALA LAAHO LIL KAAFEREENA A’LAL MOAMENEEN SABEELAA.\nThose who (keep) watch upon you; then if there be for you a victory from God say they “Are we not with you?” and if the infidels have a share (in the victory), say they “Did we not acquire mastery over you and defend you from the believers?” Therefore God shall judge between you on the Dry of Resurrection; And never will God make for the infidels a way (to triumph) against the believers.\nاِنَّ الْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ يُخٰدِعُوْنَ اللّٰهَ وَهُوَ خَادِعُوْهُمْ ۚ وَاِذَا قَامُوْۤا اِلَى الصَّلٰوةِ قَامُوْا كُسَالٰى ۙ يُرَآءُوْنَ النَّاسَ وَلَا يَذْكُرُوْنَ اللّٰهَ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا ۙ‏(142)\nINNAL MONAAFEQEENA YOKHAADE-O’ONAL LAAHA WA HOWA KHAADEU’OOHUM WA EZAA QAAMOOA ELAL AS-SALAAWTE QAAMOOA KUSAALAA YORAAA-OONA NAASA WA LAA YAZKUROONA LAAHA ILLAA QALEELAA.\nVerily the hypocrites strive to deceive God while He is deceiving them; and when they stand up for prayer, they stand up sluggishly (without earnestness) they do it only to be seen of men, and they remember not God save a little.\nمُّذَبْذَبِيْنَ بَيْنَ  ۖ ذٰ لِكَ لَاۤ اِلٰى هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ وَلَاۤ اِلٰى هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ ؕ وَمَنْ يُّضْلِلِ اللّٰهُ فَلَنْ تَجِدَ لَهٗ سَبِيْلًا‏(143)\nMMUZABZABEENA BAYNA ZAA LEKA LAA ELAA HAAOOLAAA-E WA LAA ELAA HAAOOLAAA-E WA MAN YYUZLELE LAAHO FALAN TAJEDA LAHU SABEELAA.\nWavering between that (and this); Neither towards these (believers) nor towards those (infidels); And whoever God leaveth to go astray, never then shall thou find for him a way.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَتَّخِذُوا الْكٰفِرِيْنَ اَوْلِيَآءَ مِنْ دُوْنِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ ؕ اَ تُرِيْدُوْنَ اَنْ تَجْعَلُوْا لِلّٰهِ عَلَيْكُمْ سُلْطٰنًا مُّبِيْنًا‏(144)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TATTAKHEZOOA KAAFEREEN AAWLEEAAAA MIN DOONIL MOAMENEEN A’ZAABAN TOREEDOONA AN TAJ-A’LOO LILLAAHE A’LAYKUM SULTAANAN MOBEENAA.\nO’ ye who believe! take not the disbelievers for friends rather than the believers; Desire ye to furnish unto God against yourselves a manifest authority (proof) (to punish you)?\nاِنَّ الْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ فِى الدَّرْكِ الْاَسْفَلِ مِنَ النَّارِ ۚ وَلَنْ تَجِدَ لَهُمْ نَصِيْرًا ۙ‏(145)\nINNAL MONAAFEQEENA FIL AD-DARKE AL-AASFALE MENAL NAAR WA LAN TAJEDA LAHUM NASEERAA.\nVerily the hypocrites shall be in the lowest stage of the (Hell) fire, and never shalt thou find for them a helper.\nاِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ تَابُوْا وَاَصْلَحُوْا وَاعْتَصَمُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَاَخْلَصُوْا دِيْنَهُمْ لِلّٰهِ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ مَعَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ ؕ وَسَوْفَ يُؤْتِ اللّٰهُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ اَجْرًا عَظِيْمًا‏(146)\nILLAA LAZEENA TAABOO WA ASLAHOO WAAA’TASAMOOA BIL-LAAHE WAAKHLASOOA DEENAHUM LILLAAHE FA-OOLAAA-EKA LAAHA MOAMENEEN WA SAWFA YUTE LAAHO MOAMENEEN AJRAN A’ZEEMAA.\nExcept those who repent, and Amend (themselves) and hold fast to God and purify their religion (wholly) for God, these then shall be with the (true) believers; and anon will God give the believers a great reward.\nمَا يَفْعَلُ اللّٰهُ بِعَذَابِكُمْ اِنْ شَكَرْتُمْ وَاٰمَنْتُمْ ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ شَاكِرًا عَلِيْمًا‏(147)\nMAA YAF-A’LO LAAHO BEA’AZAABEKUM IN SHAKARTUM WA AAMANTUM KAANAL LAAHO SHAAKERAWN A’LEEMAN.\nWhat hath God to do to torment you, if ye be grateful and ye believe? While God is the (greatest) Appreciator (of worth) and the All-Knowing.\nلَا يُحِبُّ اللّٰهُ الْجَهْرَ بِالسُّوْٓءِ مِنَ الْقَوْلِ اِلَّا مَنْ ظُلِمَؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ سَمِيْعًا عَلِيْمًا‏(148)\nLAA YOHIBBUL LAAHO JAHRA BIS-SOOO-E MENAL AL-QAWLE ILLAA MAN ZULEMA KAANAL LAAHO SAMEE-A’M A’LEEMAN.\nLoveth not God, open utterance of evil in speech except by one who hath been wronged; And God is the Hearer, the Knower.\nاِنْ تُبْدُوْا خَيْرًا اَوْ تُخْفُوْهُ اَوْ تَعْفُوْا عَنْ سُوْٓءٍ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ عَفُوًّا قَدِيْرًا‏(149)\nIN IN TUBDOO KHAYRAN AW TUKHFOOHO AW TAA’FOOA A’N SOOO-IN FA-INNAL LAAHA KAANA A’AFOOA QADEERAA.\nIf ye do good openly or conceal it, or pardon an evil, then Verily, God is Pardoning, Powerful.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يَكْفُرُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَرُسُلِهٖ وَيُرِيْدُوْنَ اَنْ يُّفَرِّقُوْا بَيْنَ اللّٰهِ وَرُسُلِهٖ وَيَقُوْلُوْنَ نُؤْمِنُ بِبَعْضٍ وَّنَكْفُرُ بِبَعْضٍۙ وَّيُرِيْدُوْنَ اَنْ يَّتَّخِذُوْا بَيْنَ ذٰ لِكَ سَبِيْلًا ۙ‏(150)\nINNAL LAZEENA YAKFOROON BIL-LAAHE WA ROSOLEHI WA YOREEDOONA AN YYUFARREQOOA BAYNA LAAHE WA ROSOLEHI WA YAQOOLOONA NOAMENO BE-BA’Z WWANAKFURU BE-BA’Z WWAYUREEDOONA AN YYATTAKHEZOOA BAYNA ZAA LEKA SABEELAA.\nVerily those who deny God and His apostles and desire that they differentiate between God and His apostles and say, “We believe in some and we deny some”, intend they to take between (this and) that a (midway).\nاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ حَقًّا ۚ وَ اَعْتَدْنَا لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ عَذَابًا مُّهِيْنًا‏(151)\nOOLAAA-EKA HOMUL KAAFEROON HAQQAN WA A-A’TADNAA LIL KAAFEREENA A’ZAABAN MOHEENAA.\nThese are they the infidels truly, and We have prepared for the infidels a disgraceful torment.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَرُسُلِهٖ وَلَمْ يُفَرِّقُوْا بَيْنَ اَحَدٍ مِّنْهُمْ اُولٰٓئِكَ سَوْفَ يُؤْتِيْهِمْ اُجُوْرَهُمْ ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ غَفُوْرًا رَّحِيْمًا‏(152)\nWAL LAZEENA AAMANOO BIL-LAAHE WA ROSOLEHI WA LAM YUFARREQOOA BAYNA AHADIM MINHUM OOLAAA-EKA SAWFA YUTEEHEM AUJOORAHUM KAANAL LAAHO GHAFOORAR RAHEEMAA.\nAnd they who believe in God and His apostles and differentiate not between anyone of them, they, (are those whom) He will grant them their recompense; And God is Oft-Forgiving, Merciful.\nيَسْئَلُكَ اَهْلُ الْكِتٰبِ اَنْ تُنَزِّلَ عَلَيْهِمْ كِتٰبًا مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ فَقَدْ سَاَ لُوْا مُوْسٰٓى اَكْبَرَ مِنْ ذٰ لِكَ فَقَالُوْۤا اَرِنَا اللّٰهَ جَهْرَةً فَاَخَذَتْهُمُ الصّٰعِقَةُ بِظُلْمِهِمْ ۚ ثُمَّ اتَّخَذُوا الْعِجْلَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا جَآءَتْهُمُ الْبَيِّنٰتُ فَعَفَوْنَا عَنْ ذٰ لِكَ ۚ وَاٰتَيْنَا مُوْسٰى سُلْطٰنًا مُّبِيْنًا‏(153)\nYAS-ALOKAN AAHLU KETAABE AN TUNAZZELA A’LAYHIM KETAABAA MENAL SAMAAA-E FAQAD HAQ LOOA MOOSAA AAKBARA MIN ZAA LEKA FA-QAALOO ARENAL LAAHA JAHRATN FA-AKHAZATHOMUR SAA-E’QATO BEZULMEHEM SUMMA ATTAKHAZOOA I’JLA MIN BA’DE MAA JAAA-ATHOMUL BAYYENAATO FA A’FAWNAA A’N ZAA LEKA WA AATAYNAA MOOSAA SULTAANAN MOBEENAA.\nThe people of the Book ask thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) to get descended upon them a book from heaven; so indeed they had demanded of Moses (a) greater (thing) than that, for they said “Show us God manifestly” whereupon seized them a rumbling for their wickedness; Then they took a calf (for a god) even after what clear signs had come unto them, but (even then) We pardoned them (for) this; and We gave Moses a clear authority.\nوَرَفَعْنَا فَوْقَهُمُ الطُّوْرَ بِمِيْثَاقِهِمْ وَقُلْنَا لَهُمُ ادْخُلُوا الْبَابَ سُجَّدًا وَّقُلْنَا لَهُمْ لَا تَعْدُوْا فِى السَّبْتِ وَاَخَذْنَا مِنْهُمْ مِّيْثَاقًا غَلِيْظًا‏(154)\nWA RAFA’NAA FAWQAHUMU FAWQAKOMUT BEMEESAAQEHEM WA LAHOMUL ADKHULOOA BAABA SUJJADANW WWAQULNAA LAHUM LAA TAA’DOOA FIL SABTE AKHAZNAA MINHUM MMEESAAQAN GHALEEZAA.\nAnd We lifted up the Mountain over them at their covenant and said We unto them “Enter the door prostrating” and said We unto them “Exceed not (Our limits) in the Sabath (day)” and We took from them a firm Covenant.\nفَبِمَا نَقْضِهِمْ مِّيْثَاقَهُمْ وَكُفْرِهِمْ بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ وَقَتْلِهِمُ الْاَنْۢبِيَآءَ بِغَيْرِ حَقٍّ وَّقَوْلِهِمْ قُلُوْبُنَا غُلْفٌ ؕ بَلْ طَبَعَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهَا بِكُفْرِهِمْ فَلَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا‏(155)\nFA BEMAA NAQZEHEM MMEESAAQAHUM WAKUFREHEM BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE WAQATLEHEMU AL-AANBEEAAAA BEGHAYRIL HAQQIN WWAQAWLEHEM QOLOOBONAA GHULFUN BAL TABAA’A LAAHO A’LAYHAA BEKUFREHIM FALAA YOAMENOONA ILLAA QALEELAA.\nSo for their breaking their covenant and their denial of the signs of God, and their slaying the apostles unjustly and their saying “Our hearts are covered;” Nay! God hath set a seal upon them for their disbelief, so they believe not but a little.\nوَّبِكُفْرِهِمْ وَقَوْلِهِمْ عَلٰى مَرْيَمَ بُهْتَانًا عَظِيْمًا ۙ‏(156)\nWWABEKUFREHEM WA QAWLEHIM A’LAA MARYAMAL BOHTAANANW A’ZEEMAA.\nAnd for their disbelief and for their utterance against Mary a grievous calumny.\nوَّقَوْلِهِمْ اِنَّا قَتَلْنَا الْمَسِيْحَ عِيْسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ رَسُوْلَ اللّٰهِ ۚ وَمَا قَتَلُوْهُ وَمَا صَلَبُوْهُ وَلٰكِنْ شُبِّهَ لَهُمْ ؕ وَاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اخْتَلَفُوْا فِيْهِ لَفِىْ شَكٍّ مِّنْهُ ؕ مَا لَهُمْ بِهٖ مِنْ عِلْمٍ اِلَّا اتِّبَاعَ الظَّنِّ ۚ وَمَا قَتَلُوْهُ يَقِيْنًا ۢ ۙ‏(157)\nWWAQAWLEHEM INNAA QATALNAA AL-MASEEHA E’ESAB NA MARYAMAL TOAZOO LAAHE WA MAA QATALOOHU WA MAA SALABOOHU WA LAAKIL SHUBBEHA LAHUM WA INNA LAZEENA TALAFOO FEEHE LAFEE SHAKKIM MINHO MAA LAHUM BEHI MIN I’LMIN ILLAA ATTEBAAA’A AZ-ZANNE WA MAA QATALOOHU YAQEENAN.\nAnd for their saying (in boast) “Verily we have slain the Messiah, Jesus, son of Mary, the Apostle of God;” But they slew him not, and they crucified him not but (it ) became dubious unto them; and indeed those who differ therein are only in doubt about it they have no knowledge about the (real) matter, pursuing (only) a conjecture; and certainly, they slew him not.\nبَلْ رَّفَعَهُ اللّٰهُ اِلَيْهِ ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ عَزِيْزًا حَكِيْمًا‏(158)\nBAL RRAFAA’AHU LAAHO ELAYHE KAANAL LAAHO A’ZEEZAA HAKEEMAA.\nNay! God raised (lifted) him up unto Himself; And God is Mighty, Wise!\nوَاِنْ مِّنْ اَهْلِ الْكِتٰبِ اِلَّا لَيُؤْمِنَنَّ بِهٖ قَبْلَ مَوْتِهٖ ۚ وَيَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ يَكُوْنُ عَلَيْهِمْ شَهِيْدًا ۚ‏(159)\nWA MIN AHLIL KETAABE ILLAA LAYUMENANNA BEHI QABLA MAWTEH WA YAWMA QEYAAMATE LAHUL A’LAYHIM SHAHEEDAA.\nAnd there shall not be any one of the people of the book, but he must certainly believe in him before his death; and on the Day of Resurrection, he (Jesus) will be a witness against them.\nفَبِظُلْمٍ مِّنَ الَّذِيْنَ هَادُوْا حَرَّمْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ طَيِّبٰتٍ اُحِلَّتْ لَهُمْ وَبِصَدِّهِمْ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ كَثِيْرًا ۙ‏(160)\nFABEZULMIN MENAL LAZEENA HAADOO HARRAMNAA A’LAYHIM TAYBAATIN AUHELLAT LAHUM WABESADDEHEM A’N SABEELIL LAAHE KASEERAA.\nFor the iniquity from those who Judaize, we did forbid them those good things which had been made lawful for them (before), and for their obstructing many (people) from the path of God.\nوَّاَخْذِهِمُ الرِّبٰوا وَقَدْ نُهُوْا عَنْهُ وَاَكْلِهِمْ اَمْوَالَ النَّاسِ بِالْبَاطِلِ ؕ وَاَعْتَدْنَا لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ مِنْهُمْ عَذَابًا اَ لِيْمًا‏(161)\nWWAAKHZEHEMU REBAA WA QAD NUHOOA A’NHO WAAKLEHEM AAMWAALA NAASE BIL-BAATELE WA A-ATADNAA LIL KAAFEREENA MINHUM A’ZAABAN A’ZAABAN ALEEMAA.\nAnd (for) their taking interest, though indeed forbidden were they against it, and their devouring people’s property wrongfully; and We have (got) prepared for the disbelievers from among them a painful torment.\nلٰكِنِ الرّٰسِخُوْنَ فِى الْعِلْمِ مِنْهُمْ وَالْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكَ وَمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ مِنْ قَبْلِكَ وَالْمُقِيْمِيْنَ الصَّلٰوةَ وَالْمُؤْتُوْنَ الزَّكٰوةَ وَ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ سَنُؤْتِيْهِمْ اَجْرًا عَظِيْمًا‏(162)\nLAAKENE AR-RAASEKHOONA FIL I’LME MINHUM WAL MO’MENOONA YOAMENOONA BEMAA UNZELA ELAYKA WA MAA UNZELA MIN QABLEKA WAL MUQEEMEENA SALAATA WAL MUTOONA ZAKAATA WA MOAMENOONA BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE OOLAAA-EKA SANUTEEHEM AJRAN A’ZEEMAA.\nBut the well-grounded in knowledge among them and the believers (who) believe in what hath been sent down unto thee and what hath been sent down (unto Our apostles) before thee, and the establishers of prayer, and the givers of the poor-rate (charity), and the believers in God and the Last Day (of Judgment); These (it is whom) soon We will give a great recompense.\nاِنَّاۤ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ كَمَاۤ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلٰى نُوْحٍ وَّالنَّبِيّٖنَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ ۚ وَاَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلٰٓى اِبْرٰهِيْمَ وَاِسْمٰعِيْلَ وَاِسْحٰقَ وَيَعْقُوْبَ وَالْاَسْبَاطِ وَعِيْسٰى وَاَيُّوْبَ وَيُوْنُسَ وَهٰرُوْنَ وَسُلَيْمٰنَ ۚ وَاٰتَيْنَا دَاوٗدَ زَبُوْرًا ۚ‏(163)\nINNAA AAWHAYNAA ELAYKA KAMAA AAWHAYNAA ELAA NOOHIN WWAALNNABEENA MIN BA’DEHI WA AWHAYNAA ELAA IBRAAHEEMA WA ISMAA-E’ELA WA ISHAAQA WA YA’QOOBA WA ASBAATE WA E’ESAA WAAYYOOBA WAYOONUSA WA AALO WA SOLAYMAANA WA AATAYNAA DAAWOODA ZABOORAN.\nVerily, We have revealed unto thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) as We did reveal unto Noah and the Apostles after him; We did reveal unto Abraham, and Ishmael and Isaac and Jacob and the Tribes, and Jesus and Job and Jonah, and Aaron, and Solomon, and gave We to David the Psalms.\nوَرُسُلًا قَدْ قَصَصْنٰهُمْ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ قَبْلُ وَرُسُلًا لَّمْ نَقْصُصْهُمْ عَلَيْكَ ؕ وَكَلَّمَ اللّٰهُ مُوْسٰى تَكْلِيْمًا ۚ‏(164)\nWA ROSOLAN QAD QASASNAAHUM A’LAYKA MIN QABLO WA ROSOLAN LAM NAQSUSHUM A’LAYKA WA KALLAMAL LAAHO MOOSAA TAKLEEMAN.\nAnd apostles We have (already) mentioned unto thee before and Apostles We mentioned not unto thee; and God spake unto Moses, directly discoursing.\nرُسُلًا مُّبَشِّرِيْنَ وَمُنْذِرِيْنَ لِئَلَّا يَكُوْنَ لِلنَّاسِ عَلَى اللّٰهِ حُجَّةٌ ۢ بَعْدَ الرُّسُلِ ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ عَزِيْزًا حَكِيْمًا‏(165)\nROSOLAN MMUBASSHEREENA WA MUNZEREEN LE-ALLAA YAKOONA LIN-NAASE A’LAL LAAHE HUJJATUN BA’DA AR-RUSULE KAANAL LAAHO A’ZEEZAA HAKEEMAA.\n(We sent) apostles as givers of glad tidings and warners, that there may not remain any argument for people against God, after (the coming of) these apostles, And God is Mighty, Wise.\nلٰكِنِ اللّٰهُ يَشْهَدُ بِمَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اِلَيْكَ اَنْزَلَهٗ بِعِلْمِهٖ ۚ وَالْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ يَشْهَدُوْنَ ؕ وَكَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ شَهِيْدًا ؕ‏(166)\nLAAKENE LAAHO YASHHADO BEMAA ANZALAL ELAYKA ELAYKUM BE-I’LMEHI WAL MALAAA-EKATO YASHHADOONA KAFAA BIL-LAAHE SHAHEEDAA.\nBut God (Himself) beareth Witness, that what He hath sent down unto thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!), sent He that down, with His knowledge; and the Angels (too) bear witness; and sufficient is God for a Witness.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَ صَدُّوْا عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ قَدْ ضَلُّوْا ضَلٰلًاۢ بَعِيْدًا‏(167)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO WA SADDOOA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE QAD ZALLOOA ZALAALAM BAE’EEDAN.\nVerily those who disbelieve and obstruct (people) from God’s way, indeed have they strayed off, far away (from the Right Path).\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَظَلَمُوْا لَمْ يَكُنِ اللّٰهُ لِيَغْفِرَ لَهُمْ وَلَا لِيَهْدِيَهُمْ طَرِيْقًا ۙ‏(168)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO WA ZALAMOO LAM YAKONIL LAAHO LEEGHFERA LAHUM WA LAA LEEHDEEHUM TAREEQAN.\nVerily, those who disbelieve and act unjustly, it is not for God to pardon them, nor is it that He will guide them to a way.\nاِلَّا طَرِيْقَ جَهَنَّمَ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَاۤ اَبَدًا ؕ وَكَانَ ذٰ لِكَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ يَسِيْرًا‏(169)\nILLAA TAREEQA JAHANNAMA KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ABADAM KAANAL ZAA LEKA A’LAL LAAHE YASEERAA.\nExcept the way to Hell, to abide therein for ever! And this, for God is easy.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ قَدْ جَآءَكُمُ الرَّسُوْلُ بِالْحَقِّ مِنْ رَّبِّكُمْ فَاٰمِنُوْا خَيْرًا لَّكُمْ ؕ وَاِنْ تَكْفُرُوْا فَاِنَّ لِلّٰهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ عَلِيْمًا حَكِيْمًا‏(170)\nYAA AYYOHAL NAASO QAD JAAAKUMU RASOOLO BIL-HAQQE MIN RABBEKUM FA AAMENOO KHAYRAN LAKUM WA TAKFUROOA FA-INNAL LILLAAHE MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE KAANAL LAAHO A’LEEMAN HAKEEMAA.\nO’ mankind! Verily, the Apostle (Muhammad) hath come unto you with truth from your Lord; Believe (then) (in him), it is good for you; and if ye disbelieve, then, God’s is whatever in the Heavens and the Earth; and God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.\nيٰۤاَهْلَ الْكِتٰبِ لَا تَغْلُوْا فِىْ دِيْنِكُمْوَلَا تَقُوْلُوْا عَلَى اللّٰهِ اِلَّا الْحَقَّ ؕ اِنَّمَا الْمَسِيْحُ عِيْسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ رَسُوْلُ اللّٰهِ وَكَلِمَتُهٗ ۚ اَ لْقٰٮهَاۤ اِلٰى مَرْيَمَ وَرُوْحٌ مِّنْهُ فَاٰمِنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَرُسُلِهٖ ۚ وَلَا تَقُوْلُوْا ثَلٰثَةٌ ؕ اِنْتَهُوْا خَيْرًا لَّكُمْ ؕ اِنَّمَا اللّٰهُ اِلٰهٌ وَّاحِدٌ ؕ سُبْحٰنَهٗۤ اَنْ يَّكُوْنَ لَهٗ وَلَدٌ ۘ لَهٗ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِؕ وَكَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ وَكِيْلًا‏(171)\nYAA AHLA KETAABE LAA TAGHLOOA FEE DEENEKUMWALAA TAQOOLOO A’LAL LAAHE ILLAA HAQQA INNAMAA AL-MASEEHU E’ESAB ABNU MARYAMAL RASOOLAL LAAHE WAKALEMATUH A’ZAABAN LQAAHAA ELAA MARYAMAL WAROOHUN MINHO FA AAMENOO BIL-LAAHE WA ROSOLEHI WA LAA TAQOOLOO SALAASATUN AENTAHOOA KHAYRAN LAKUM INNAMAA LAAHO ELAAHUN WAAHED WALADAN AN YAKOONA LAHU WALADUN LAHU MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZ KAFAA BIL-LAAHE WAKEELAA.\nO’ People of the Book! overstep not in your religion, and say not upon God except the Truth; Verily, Verily, the Messiah Jesus, son of Mary, is only an apostle of God and His Word which He conveyed unto Mary, and a Spirit (Proceeding) from Him; Believe therefore in God, and His apostles, and say not (that there are) Three (gods) Desist! It is good for you; Verily, Verily, God! (there is) Only One God! Far be it from His (Absolute)-Purity that there be for Him a son; His is whatever is in the Heavens and whatever is in the Earth; God is sufficient as a Protector.\nلَنْ يَّسْتَنْكِفَ الْمَسِيْحُ اَنْ يَّكُوْنَ عَبْدًا لِّلَّهِ وَلَا الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ الْمُقَرَّبُوْنَؕ وَمَنْ يَّسْتَنْكِفْ عَنْ عِبَادَ تِهٖ وَيَسْتَكْبِرْ فَسَيَحْشُرُهُمْ اِلَيْهِ جَمِيْعًا‏(172)\nLAN YYASTANKEFA AL-MASEEHU AN YAKOONA A’BDAN LILLAAH WA LAA TAHMELOHUL MOQARRABOON WA MAN YYASTANKEF A’N E’BAADAL TEH WAYASTAKBER FASAYAHSHURUHUM ELAYHE JAMEE-A’A.\nNever doth Christ disdain to be a slave unto God, nor do the Angels (who are) near (unto Him); and whosoever disdaineth against His service, and prideth, He will gather them unto Him, all together.\nفَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ فَيُوَفِّيْهِمْ اُجُوْرَهُمْ وَ يَزِيْدُهُمْ مِّنْ فَضْلِهٖۚ وَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ اسْتَنْكَفُوْا وَاسْتَكْبَرُوْا فَيُعَذِّبُهُمْ عَذَابًا اَ لِيْمًا  ۙ وَّلَا يَجِدُوْنَ لَهُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَلِيًّا وَّلَا نَصِيْرًا‏(173)\nFA-AMMAA LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE FAYOOFFEEHEM AUJOORAHUM WA YAZEEDUHUM MIN FAZLEHI WA AMMAA LAZEENA ASTANKAFOOA WAASTAKBAROOA FAYUA’AZZEBUHUM A’ZAABAN A’ZAABAN ALEEMAA WA LAA YAJEDOONA LAHUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE WALIYYANW WA LAA NASEERAA.\nAnd (then as for) those who believe and do good (deeds), He will pay them fully their, (due) recompense, and increase them of His Grace, and as for those who disdain and are proud, He will chastise them with a painful torment. And they shall find not for themselves besides God, any guardian or helper.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ قَدْ جَآءَكُمْ بُرْهَانٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ وَاَنْزَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْكُمْ نُوْرًا مُّبِيْنًا‏(174)\nYAA AYYOHAL NAASO QAD JAAA-AKUM BURHAANUN MIN RABBEKUM WA ANZALNAA ELAYKUM NOORAN MOBEENAA.\nO’ mankind! Indeed hath come unto you (an undeniable) proof from your Lord, and We have sent down unto you a manifest light.\nفَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَاعْتَصَمُوْا بِهٖ فَسَيُدْخِلُهُمْ فِىْ رَحْمَةٍ مِّنْهُ وَفَضْلٍۙ وَّيَهْدِيْهِمْ اِلَيْهِ صِرَاطًا مُّسْتَقِيْمًا ؕ‏(175)\nFA-AMMAA LAZEENA AAMANOO BIL-LAAHE WAAA’TASAMOOA BEHI FASAYUDKHELUHUM FEE RAHMATIN MINHO WA FAZLIN WWAYAHDEEHEM ELAYHE SERAATAM MUSTAQEEMAA.\nThen as for those who believe in God and hold fast unto Him, soon will He admit them to Mercy from Him and (His) Grace; and guide them unto Himself (by) the Straight Way.\nيَسْتَفْتُوْنَكَ ؕ قُلِ اللّٰهُ يُفْتِيْكُمْ فِى الْكَلٰلَةِ ؕ اِنِ امْرُؤٌا هَلَكَ لَيْسَ لَهٗ وَلَدٌ وَّلَهٗۤ اُخْتٌ فَلَهَا نِصْفُ مَا تَرَكَ ۚ وَهُوَ يَرِثُهَاۤ اِنْ لَّمْ يَكُنْ لَّهَا وَلَدٌ  ؕ فَاِنْ كَانَتَا اثْنَتَيْنِ فَلَهُمَا الثُّلُثٰنِ مِمَّا تَرَكَ ؕ وَاِنْ كَانُوْۤا اِخْوَةً رِّجَالًا وَّنِسَآءً فَلِلذَّكَرِ مِثْلُ حَظِّ الْاُنْثَيَيْنِ ؕ يُبَيِّنُ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ اَنْ تَضِلُّوْا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(176)\nYASTAFTOONAKA QOLIL LAAHO YUFTEEKUM FIL AL-KALAALATE ENIS AMRUUNA HALAKA LAYSA LAHU WALADUN WWALAH AUKHTUN FA LAHAA NESFU MAA TARAKA WA HOWA YARESUHAA IN LAM YAKUL LLAHAA WALADUN FA-IN KAANATAA ASNATAYNE FA LAHOMAA AS-SULUSAANE MIMMAA TARAKA WA KAANOO AEKHWATAN RREJAALAN WWANESAAAN FALELZZAKARE LAZEE HAZZE AL-AUNSAYAYNE YOBAYYENUL LAAHO LAKUM AN TAZELLOOA WAL LAAHO BEKULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEM.\nThey ask thee for a decree (about the Law): Say, (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) God giveth you a decision about ‘Kalala ‘ the side kindred; If a man dieth (and) there be for him no offspring, and for him be a sister, for her shall be half of what he leaveth; and he shall be her heir, if there not be for her a son; and if there be two sisters, then for them (two) shall be two thirds of what he leaveth; and if there be brethren, men and women, then for the male shall be the like of the shares of two females; God maketh it clear for you, lest ye err, and God is the Knower of all things.",
